CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 1-2 (Exceptions to Sale or Gift)
"Transfer of ownership prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 2 (1) 8-2 of the Act means any of the following transfers of ownership:
1. A transfer of ownership by inheritance;
2. A transfer of ownership resulting from the expropriation of real estate under other Acts, such as the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land for Public Works Projects: Provided, That this shall exclude cases where real estate is acquired after public notice of project approval under Article 22 of that Act (including cases where such public notice applies mutatis mutandis or is deemed given under another Act), or public notice, etc. by an administrative agency equivalent to such public notice of project approval under another Act, and is subsequently expropriated;
3. A transfer of ownership of trust property on which acquisition tax is not imposed under Article 9 (3) of the Local Tax Act.

Article 2 (Scale of Local Tax Reductions and Exemptions)
(1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 4 (2) of the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means any of the following cases in which the Minister of the Interior and Safety recognizes the need for a reduction of or exemption from local taxes (meaning a reduction of or exemption from local taxes under Article 4 (1) of the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article): <Added on January 15, 2020; March 14, 2023>
1. Where necessary for responding to and recovering from a disaster under subparagraph 1 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety;
2. Where necessary for overcoming a national or local economic crisis, such as an economic recession or mass unemployment;
3. Where necessary for protecting socially vulnerable groups, including persons with disabilities;
4. Where it is intended to add a tax category eligible for reduction or exemption (excluding local income tax) for persons eligible for special local income tax treatment under Chapter III of the Act who are not eligible for reductions or exemptions under Chapter II of the Act;
5. Where necessary for implementing major priority projects of the relevant local government.
(2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 4 (2) 5 of the Act means any of the following matters: <Amended on March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; March 27, 2017; July 26, 2017; January 15, 2020; December 29, 2023>
1. Matters for which the due date for payment of local taxes under the Framework Act on Local Taxes, the Local Tax Collection Act, or the Local Tax Act has passed;
2. Matters having a material impact on local tax policies under the Framework Act on Local Taxes, the Local Tax Collection Act, the Local Tax Act, the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, or the Act;
3. Matters contrary to policies on real estate, including land, social welfare policies, including the protection of socially vulnerable groups, or other major national policies;
4. Other matters that hinder the implementation of local tax policies, such as a significant impairment of equity in local tax burdens among residents of a local government.
(3) "At least a certain scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 4 (3) of the Act means, where a new local tax reduction or exemption is to be introduced, a case where the estimated amount of local tax reductions or exemptions expected during the reduction or exemption period for each provision on local tax reduction or exemption in the proposed ordinance is at least three billion won (one billion won for a Si, Gun, or autonomous Gu); and, where a local tax reduction or exemption is to be extended or modified, a case where the annual average amount of local tax reductions or exemptions for the three years immediately preceding the year in which falls the expiry date of the reduction or exemption under the relevant ordinance, or the date determined by the head of the relevant local government for the proposed ordinance modifying the local tax reduction or exemption (or the actual period if three years have not elapsed since its introduction), is at least three billion won (one billion won for a Si, Gun, or autonomous Gu). <Amended on December 29, 2017; December 31, 2018; January 15, 2020; December 29, 2023>
(4) "Tax-related specialized institution, corporation, or organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 4 (3) of the Act means any of the following institutions, corporations, or organizations: <Amended on March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; March 27, 2017; July 26, 2017; January 15, 2020>
1. The local tax research institute under Article 151 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes;
2. A tax-related institution or corporation established under an Act other than the Civil Act;
3. A corporation established under the Civil Act, such as a tax-related academic society;
4. A school under Article 2 of the Higher Education Act that offers a tax-related curriculum;
5. A corporation or organization having at least two persons with at least 15 years of experience in tax-related affairs;
6. Any other institution, corporation, or organization determined and publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety.
(5) "Special grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 4 (4) of the Act means earthquakes, wind or flood damage, lightning, war damage, or similar disasters. <Amended on December 31, 2015; January 15, 2020; January 5, 2021>
(6) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from local taxes under Article 4 (4) of the Act shall, within 30 days from the date on which the relevant grounds arise, apply for the reduction or exemption to the competent Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Special Self-Governing Province Governor (meaning the Governor of a Special Self-Governing Province that has no Si or Gun constituting a local government within its jurisdiction), or head of a Si, Gun, or Gu (the head of a Gu means the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter collectively referred to as the "head of a Si/Gun/Gu"), together with documents substantiating those grounds. <Amended on December 30, 2016; January 15, 2020; December 31, 2024>
(7) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems it necessary to grant a reduction of or exemption from local taxes under Article 4 (4) of the Act, he or she may investigate persons eligible for such reduction or exemption ex officio. <Amended on December 30, 2016; January 15, 2020>
(8) "A certain ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 4 (6) of the Act means a ratio determined and publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety within five percent, taking into account the financial circumstances and the scale of local tax revenue of local governments. In such cases, where there are local tax reductions or exemptions under the proviso to the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 4 (2) of the Act (limited to local tax reductions or exemptions separately determined by the Minister of the Interior and Safety), or local tax reductions or exemptions prescribed by ordinance of a local government in consultation with the Minister of the Interior and Safety in any of the following cases, the Minister of the Interior and Safety may separately add and publicly notify a ratio reflecting the scale of such reductions or exemptions to the ratio publicly notified under the former part (the sum of the ratios shall not exceed five percent): <Amended on March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; January 15, 2020; December 31, 2025>
1. Where necessary for responding to and recovering from a disaster under subparagraph 1 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety;
2. Where necessary for resolving a national issue affecting several local governments;
3. Where necessary for supporting national infrastructure located in a specific region;
4. Where necessary for supporting special zones, complexes, etc. designated under an Act enacted to foster a specific industry;
5. Where necessary for enhancing economic vitality in depopulation areas;
6. Other cases recognized by the Minister of the Interior and Safety as similar to those under subparagraphs 1 through 5.
(9) Where the amount of local taxes reduced or exempted under an ordinance referred to in Article 4 (6) of the Act exceeds the scale of local tax reductions and exemptions for the relevant year (meaning the scale of local tax reductions and exemptions under Article 4 (6) of the Act; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph), an amount equivalent to twice the excess shall be deducted from the scale of local tax reductions and exemptions for the year after the following year, pursuant to Article 4 (7) of the Act. <Amended on January 15, 2020; December 29, 2023; December 31, 2025>

CHAPTER II REDUCTIONS AND EXEMPTIONS

SECTION 1 SUPPORT FOR AGRICULTURE AND FISHERIES

Article 3 (Criteria for Self-Cultivating Farmers and Farmland Cultivated Directly)
(1) "A person whose principal occupation is agriculture and who has engaged in farming for at least two years, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 6 (1) of the Act means a person for whom at least one of the person or his or her spouse [limited to cases where they are entered together in the resident registration record for each household under Article 7 of the Resident Registration Act (hereinafter referred to as the "household resident registration record"); hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article] meets all the following requirements as of the acquisition date: <Amended on August 20, 2014; December 30, 2014; December 31, 2015; December 30, 2016; January 15, 2020; April 28, 2020; December 31, 2020; December 31, 2024>
1. He or she shall have directly engaged in agriculture continuously for at least two years by owning or leasing and cultivating farmland (meaning farmland under Article 21 of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act; hereinafter the same shall apply);
2. He or she shall reside in the Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province (meaning a Special Self-Governing Province that has no Si or Gun constituting a local government within its jurisdiction), Si, Gun, or Gu (meaning an autonomous Gu; hereinafter collectively referred to as a "Si/Gun/Gu") in which the farmland under subparagraph 1 is located or in an adjoining Si/Gun/Gu, or within 30 kilometers of the location of that farmland;
3. His or her non-agricultural global income for the preceding year (meaning global income under Article 4 (1) 1 of the Income Tax Act, excluding income from agriculture and forestry, income from real estate rental business under Article 45 (2) of that Act, and farm household sideline income under Article 9 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act) shall be less than the amount under Article 9 (3) 1 of the Act on the Operation of Direct Payment Programs for Enhancing Public Interest Functions of Agriculture and Rural Communities and Article 6 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of that Act.
(2) "Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 6 (1) of the Act and the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of paragraph (4) of that Article respectively means a case meeting all the following requirements: <Amended on December 31, 2011; August 20, 2014; December 30, 2016; December 31, 2018; December 31, 2020; December 31, 2021; March 14, 2023>
1. The farmland and forest land shall be located outside an urban area under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (excluding development restriction zones and green areas; hereinafter referred to as an "urban area" in this paragraph and paragraph (4));
2. The address of the person acquiring the farmland and forest land shall be in the Si/Gun/Gu in which the farmland and forest land are located, in an adjoining Si/Gun/Gu, or within 30 kilometers of their location;
3. The total area of farmland and forest land owned by the person or his or her spouse (including farmland and forest land in urban areas) and farmland and forest land newly acquired by the person or his or her spouse shall not exceed 30,000 square meters for rice paddies, dry fields, and orchards (200,000 square meters for rice paddies, dry fields, and orchards within agricultural promotion areas designated under the Farmland Act), 250,000 square meters for pasture land, and 300,000 square meters for forest land. In such cases, where there is any excess, only the excess portion shall be excluded from the reduction.
(3) "Farmland prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 6 (1) of the Act means farmland under Article 21 of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act. <Added on December 31, 2021>
(4) "Facilities meeting the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 6 (2) of the Act means agricultural facilities meeting all the following requirements: <Added on December 31, 2018; December 31, 2020; December 31, 2021>
1. The agricultural facilities shall be located outside an urban area;
2. The address of the person acquiring the agricultural facilities shall be in the Si/Gun/Gu in which those facilities are located, in an adjoining Si/Gun/Gu, or within 30 kilometers of the location of those facilities: Provided, That fixed greenhouses under Article 6 (2) 1 of the Act and facilities under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph shall not be subject to restrictions concerning location.
(5) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 6 (2) 2 of the Act means the following facilities: <Added on December 31, 2020; December 31, 2021>
1. Livestock rearing facilities, disinfection and disease prevention facilities, milking rooms, and egg collection rooms;
2. Discharge facilities under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act on the Management and Use of Livestock Excreta;
3. Purification facilities under subparagraph 7 of Article 2 of the Act on the Management and Use of Livestock Excreta.
(6) "A person returning to farming who moves to a rural area under subparagraph 5 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 6 (4) of the Act means a person meeting all the following requirements: <Added on December 30, 2010; January 1, 2013; December 22, 2015; December 31, 2015; December 29, 2017; December 31, 2018; December 31, 2020; December 31, 2021>
1. A person who has filed a move-in report under Article 16 of the Resident Registration Act for an area outside a rural area (meaning an area under subparagraph 5 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) and has continuously actually resided there from at least one year before the date of return to farming under paragraph (7);
2. A person who has not engaged in agriculture under subparagraph 1 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry for at least one continuous year immediately before the date of return to farming under paragraph (7);
3. A person who has filed a move-in report for a rural area under the Resident Registration Act and actually resides there.
(7) "Date of return to farming prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 6 (4) of the Act means the date on which a person returning to farming under paragraph (6) files a move-in report for the rural area to which he or she has newly moved and begins residing there. <Added on December 30, 2010; January 1, 2013; December 22, 2015; December 31, 2018; December 31, 2020; December 31, 2021>
(8) "Income prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 6 (4) 2 of the Act means non-agricultural global income for each taxable year (meaning global income under Article 4 (1) 1 of the Income Tax Act, excluding income from agriculture and forestry, income from real estate rental business under Article 45 (2) of that Act, and farm household sideline income under Article 9 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act). <Added on December 31, 2024>
(9) "Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 6 (4) 2 of the Act means 37 million won. <Added on December 31, 2024>
(10) Details concerning the non-agricultural global income for the preceding year under paragraph (1), detailed criteria for identifying persons who have engaged in agriculture for at least two years, non-agricultural global income for each taxable year under paragraph (8), the procedures for applying for a reduction or exemption, and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Added on August 20, 2014; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; December 31, 2018; December 31, 2020; December 31, 2021; December 31, 2024>

Article 4 (Persons Whose Principal Occupation Is Forestry)
"A person whose principal occupation is forestry, or a forestry successor, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 8 (3) of the Act means an exemplary forest manager under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Forestry and Mountain Villages Development Promotion Act or a forestry successor under subparagraph 4 of that Article.

Article 5 (Persons Whose Principal Occupation Is Fisheries and Criteria Therefor)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9 (1) of the Act means the following persons: <Amended on December 29, 2017; August 26, 2020; December 31, 2024>
1. A person seeking a reduction in acquisition tax by acquiring a fishery right, an aquaculture right, or a fishing vessel, who resides in the Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province, Si, Gun, or Gu (including a Gu that is not an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) in which the fishing vessel's port of registry and the coast adjoining the fishing ground or aquaculture farm are located (including another Si/Gun/Gu adjoining that area; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article), and for whom at least one of the person owning the fishing vessel, fishing ground, or aquaculture farm or his or her spouse (limited to cases where they are entered in the same household resident registration record; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) directly engages in fisheries (including aquaculture; hereinafter the same shall apply);
2. A person seeking a reduction in acquisition tax by acquiring land classified as a fish farm or a water tank under paragraph (3), who resides in the Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province, Si, Gun, or Gu in which the land or water tank is located, and for whom at least one of the person owning or leasing land classified as a fish farm or his or her spouse directly engages full-time in fisheries under the subparagraphs of Article 9 (1) of the Act: Provided, That a person whose non-fishery global income for the preceding year (meaning global income under Article 4 (1) 1 of the Income Tax Act, excluding income from fisheries, income from real estate rental business under Article 45 (2) of that Act, and farm household sideline income under Article 9 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act) is at least the amount under Article 64 (11) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall be excluded.
(2) "Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9 (1) of the Act means a case meeting the following requirements: <Amended on December 29, 2017; August 26, 2020>
1. The address of a person acquiring a fishery right, an aquaculture right, or a fishing vessel shall be in the Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province, Si, Gun, or Gu in which the fishing vessel's port of registry and the coast adjoining the fishing ground or aquaculture farm are located;
1-2. The address of a person acquiring land classified as a fish farm or a water tank under paragraph (3) shall be in the Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province, Si, Gun, or Gu in which the land or water tank is located;
2. For fishery rights and aquaculture rights, the aggregate area of newly acquired and already owned fishing grounds and aquaculture farms shall not exceed 10 hectares; for fishing vessels, the aggregate tonnage of newly acquired and already owned fishing vessels shall not exceed 30 tons; and for land classified as a fish farm, the aggregate area of newly acquired land classified as a fish farm and previously owned land classified as a fish farm shall not exceed 10,000 square meters. In such cases, where there is any excess, only the excess portion shall be excluded from the reduction.
(3) "Building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9 (1) of the Act means a water tank under Article 5 (1) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act. <Added on December 29, 2017>
(4) Matters concerning non-fishery global income for the preceding year under the proviso to paragraph (1) 2, procedures for applying for a reduction or exemption, and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Added on December 29, 2017>

Article 5-2 (Criteria for Agricultural Corporations)
(1) "Corporation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 11 (1) of the Act means a corporation that has registered agricultural management information under Article 4 (1) of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities (including a corporation that registers within 90 days from the date of registration of its incorporation). <Amended on December 29, 2023>
(2) "Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 11 (1) of the Act means that farmland, forest land, and agricultural facilities are located outside an urban area under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (excluding development restriction zones and green areas).
(3) "Young farmers' agricultural corporation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 11 (1) of the Act means an agricultural corporation whose representative meets all the following requirements: <Amended on December 31, 2025>
1. A person who, at the time of incorporation, qualifies as a young farmer or fisher (limited to a farmer) under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Successor Farmers and Fishers and Young Farmers and Fishers;
2. He or she shall be a controlling shareholder, etc. under Article 43 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act and the largest shareholder or the largest equity investor of the relevant corporation.

Article 5-3 (Criteria for Fisheries Corporations)
"Corporation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 12 (1) of the Act means a corporation that has registered fisheries management information under Article 4 (1) of the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities (including a corporation that registers within 90 days from the date of registration of its incorporation).

Article 6 (Scope of Public Facilities)
Public facilities and their appurtenant land, and land for public facilities under Article 13 (3) of the Act shall be buildings such as public office buildings, libraries, museums, and art museums and their appurtenant land, and roads, parks, etc. In such cases, the scope of land for public facilities shall be the confirmed area where such land has been confirmed through approval of the implementation plan, etc. for the relevant project district; where it has not been confirmed, it shall be an area equivalent to 45 percent (35 percent for an industrial complex development project) of the total area of the relevant project district. <Amended on December 31, 2024>

Article 6-2 (Ratio of Local Government Investment in Local Agricultural and Fishery Products Corporations)
"Ratio of local government investment prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 15 (2) 1 of the Act means the ratio of the amount invested by a local government (the sum of the amounts invested by the respective local governments where two or more local governments have jointly established the corporation) to the capital of a local public corporation under Article 49 of the Local Public Enterprises Act established for the smooth distribution and maintenance of appropriate prices of agricultural and fishery products (hereinafter referred to as a "local agricultural and fishery products corporation" in this Article): Provided, That where a local agricultural and fishery products corporation has issued shares under Article 53 (3) of the Local Public Enterprises Act, it means the ratio of the number of shares owned by a local government (including shares deemed to have been contributed by a local government under paragraph (4) of that Article) (the sum of the numbers of shares owned by the respective local governments where two or more local governments own shares) to the total number of issued shares.

Article 7 (Scope of Housing Improvement Projects)
"Project prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 16 (1) of the Act means a living environment improvement project under subparagraph 10 of Article 2 of the Agricultural and Fishing Villages Improvement Act. <Amended on December 31, 2021>

SECTION 2 SUPPORT FOR SOCIAL WELFARE

Article 8 (Scope of Persons with Disabilities)
(1) "Person with a disability prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 17 (1) of the Act means a person with a severe disability among persons with disabilities under the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities (hereinafter referred to as a "person with a disability" in this Article). <Amended on April 17, 2012; December 21, 2012; December 31, 2015; December 30, 2016; December 31, 2018>
1. Deleted. <December 31, 2015>
2. Deleted. <December 31, 2015>
3. Deleted. <December 31, 2015>
4. Deleted. <December 31, 2015>
(2) "Passenger vehicle prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17 (1) 1 (b) of the Act means a passenger vehicle with a seating capacity of at least seven but not more than 10 persons among motor vehicles classified as passenger vehicles under the Motor Vehicle Management Act. <Added on December 31, 2015; January 15, 2020>
(3) A motor vehicle exempt from acquisition tax and automobile tax under Article 17 (1) and (2) of the Act means a motor vehicle registered in the name of the person with a disability or jointly in the names of the person with a disability and a person who is entered in the same household resident registration record as that person with a disability and is confirmed, by the family relations register under Article 9 of the Act on Registration of Family Relations (hereinafter referred to as the "family relations register"), to have any of the following relationships with that person with a disability (for acquisition tax, limited to cases where they are confirmed to belong to the same household on the date of registration of the motor vehicle): <Amended on January 15, 2020>
1. The spouse, a lineal relative by blood, or a sibling of the person with a disability;
2. The spouse of a lineal relative by blood of the person with a disability;
3. A lineal relative by blood or a sibling of the spouse of the person with a disability.
(4) In applying paragraph (3), where both the person with a disability and the person falling under any subparagraph of that paragraph have registered as foreigners under Article 31 of the Immigration Act and have permanent resident status under Article 10-3 of that Act, the record of registered foreigners and the alien registration record under Article 34 (1) of that Act (hereinafter referred to as the "registered foreigner records, etc.") may substitute for the family relations register and the household resident registration record. <Added on January 15, 2020>
(5) Replacement acquisition under Article 17 (2) of the Act means a case where a motor vehicle exempted from acquisition tax or automobile tax under Article 17 of the Act is deregistered or its transfer is registered (meaning transfer to a person other than the person in whose name it was jointly registered with the person with a disability; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph) and another motor vehicle is acquired (including a case where, within 60 days from the date of acquisition and registration of the new vehicle, the former vehicle exempted from acquisition tax or automobile tax is deregistered or its transfer is registered). <Amended on December 31, 2018; January 15, 2020>
(6) Where a motor vehicle exempted from acquisition tax and automobile tax under Article 17 (1) and (2) of the Act falls under any of the following, it shall be deemed not to be owned, regardless of whether it remains registered in the books: <Amended on December 31, 2015; December 30, 2016; January 15, 2020>
1. A motor vehicle for which a motor vehicle dealer under the Motor Vehicle Management Act certifies that he or she has been requested to arrange the sale of the used motor vehicle: Provided, That where the used motor vehicle is returned to its owner without being sold, the owner shall be deemed to own it;
2. A motor vehicle recognized by the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu as irretrievable or unusable because it has disappeared, been destroyed, or been damaged by a natural disaster, fire, traffic accident, etc.;
3. A motor vehicle certified as scrapped by a motor vehicle dismantling and recycling business operator under the Motor Vehicle Management Act;
4. A motor vehicle exported after an export declaration has been filed with the head of a customs office under the Customs Act.

Article 8-2 (Scope of Settlement Villages for Persons Affected by Hansen's Disease)
"Area prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 17-2 (1) of the Act means an area specified in attached Table 1. <Amended on December 31, 2024>

Article 8-3 (Scope of Real Estate Used for Childcare Centers for Infants and Young Children)
(1) "Employer prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 19 (1) of the Act means an employer under Article 20 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Child Care Act. <Added on December 31, 2024>
(2) "Real estate prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 19 (2) 2 of the Act means any of the following real estate: <Amended on December 29, 2017; December 31, 2024>
1. Real estate whose owner is the spouse or a lineal relative by blood of the person using that real estate as a childcare center for infants and young children or as a kindergarten (hereinafter referred to as the "user"), where the owner directly participates in its operation;
2. Real estate jointly owned by its user and his or her spouse or lineal relative by blood;
3. Real estate whose owner is a religious organization and whose user is the representative of that religious organization or a religious corporation;
4. Real estate used as a workplace childcare center jointly established and operated by employers under the proviso to Article 14 (1) of the Child Care Act, or as a workplace childcare center established under paragraph (1) of that Article and Article 20 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of that Act, the operation of which is entrusted to a corporation, organization, or individual.

Article 8-4 (Scope of Free Welfare Facilities for Older Persons)
"Free welfare facilities for older persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20 (1) 1 of the Act means leisure welfare facilities for older persons, specialized agencies for the protection of older persons, employment support agencies for older persons, residential welfare facilities for older persons, medical welfare facilities for older persons, or home-based welfare facilities for older persons under Article 31 of the Welfare of Older Persons Act that fall under any of the following: <Amended on December 30, 2016; July 26, 2017; December 31, 2024>
1. Facilities where the State or a local government bears the full cost of admission (including the cost of use) for the residents;
2. Facilities where, among the users of the welfare facilities for older persons, persons receiving home care benefits or institutional care benefits under the Long-Term Care Insurance Act and persons receiving benefits under Article 7 (1) 1 through 3 of the National Basic Living Security Act constitute at least 80 percent of the annual average number of residents, and which meet the criteria prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.

Article 9 (Scope of Youth Organizations)
"Organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21 (1) 4 of the Act means any of the following youth organizations: <Amended on March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; October 1, 2025>
1. A youth organization that has obtained permission or authorization from the Government, or that is established under, or subject to, an Act other than the Civil Act;
2. An organization publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety in consultation with the Minister of Gender Equality and Family.

Article 10 (Scope of Businesses of Social Welfare Corporations Eligible for Exemption)
(1) "Corporation or organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22 (1) 1 of the Act means the Korea Hansen Welfare Association, an incorporated association established under Article 32 of the Civil Act. <Amended on March 14, 2023>
(2) "Corporation or organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22 (1) 2 of the Act means the following corporations or organizations: <Added on March 14, 2023>
1. A nonprofit corporation established under Article 32 of the Civil Act;
2. An organization meeting all the following requirements:
(a) It shall have general rules concerning its organization and operation;
(b) It shall have a representative or administrator;
(c) It shall independently own and manage income and property in its own name and for its own account;
(d) It shall not distribute its income to its members.
(3) "Appurtenant land of a building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 22 (3) of the Act means appurtenant land of a building to be directly used for the relevant business where the building is under construction, or appurtenant land of a planned building where construction cannot commence after a building permit has been granted because of building restrictions imposed by an administrative agency. <Amended on December 31, 2014; March 14, 2023>
(4) "License for direct use by a social welfare corporation, etc. for its business" in the main clause of Article 22 (5) of the Act means a license necessary for a social welfare corporation, etc. under the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 22 (3) of the Act to operate its nonprofit business, or a license where all proceeds arising from the business facilities or activities authorized by that license are used for its nonprofit business. <Amended on December 31, 2014; March 14, 2023>
(5) "Corporation or organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 22 (5) of the Act means the corporations or organizations under the subparagraphs of paragraph (2). <Added on March 14, 2023>
(6) "Business place portion and employee portion of resident tax prescribed by Presidential Decree in connection with profit-making business" in the proviso to Article 22 (5) of the Act means the business place portion (limited to the amount imposed under Article 81 (1) 2 of the Local Tax Act) and the employee portion of resident tax imposed on the basis of the business places and employees used for profit-making business. In such cases, where a building is used both for a business eligible for exemption and for a profit-making business, or an employee concurrently performs duties for both, the principal use or duty shall govern. <Amended on March 14, 2014; December 31, 2014; December 31, 2020; March 14, 2023>

Article 10-2 (Scope of Replacement Acquisition by Persons Raising Multiple Children)
Replacement acquisition under Article 22-2 (3) 1 of the Act means a case where a motor vehicle for which acquisition tax has been reduced or exempted under Article 22-2 of the Act is deregistered or its transfer is registered (excluding transfers between spouses; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article), and another motor vehicle is acquired (including a case where, within 60 days from the date of acquisition and registration of the new vehicle, the former vehicle for which acquisition tax was reduced or exempted is deregistered or its transfer is registered). <Amended on December 31, 2024>

Article 10-3 (Scope of Dormant Deposit Management Foundations Eligible for Exemption from Registration and License Tax)
"Person prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 22-3 of the Act means a project implementation institution under subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Act on Support for the Financial Life of the Common People. <Amended on September 22, 2016>

Article 11 (Scope of Multi-Unit Housing for Members)
"Multi-unit housing for members prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 25 (1) of the Act means multi-unit housing for members with an exclusive use area of not more than 85 square meters.

Article 12 (Definition of Self-Supporting Veterans' Villages)
"A self-supporting veterans' village for persons of distinguished service to the State, designated by the Minister of Patriots and Veterans Affairs and composed of persons assessed as having a disability of Grade 1 as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 29 (3) of the Act means a self-supporting veterans' village designated under Article 88-4 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Honorable Treatment of and Support for Persons of Distinguished Service to the State. <Amended on April 11, 2023>

Article 12-2 (Scope of Persons of Distinguished Service to the State)
(1) "Person prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 29 (4) of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended on April 6, 2021>
1. A person injured in the May 18 Democratization Movement, registered under the Act on the Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service to the May 18 Democratization Movement and Establishment of Related Organizations, who has been assessed as having a physical disability of Grade 1 through 14;
2. A patient suffering from potential aftereffects of defoliants under the Act on Assistance to Patients Suffering from Actual or Potential Aftereffects of Defoliants and Establishment of Related Organizations who has been assessed as having at least a mild disability.
(2) "Passenger vehicle prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 29 (4) 1 (b) of the Act means a passenger vehicle with a seating capacity of at least seven but not more than 10 persons among motor vehicles classified as passenger vehicles under the Motor Vehicle Management Act: Provided, That for a motor vehicle structurally modified for the mobility convenience of persons of distinguished service to the State, etc. under Article 29 (4) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "persons of distinguished service to the State, etc." in this Article), its seating capacity shall be determined based on the seating capacity before the structural modification.
(3) A motor vehicle exempt from acquisition tax and automobile tax under Article 29 (4) of the Act means a motor vehicle registered in the name of a person of distinguished service to the State, etc., or jointly in the names of that person and a person who is entered in the same household resident registration record as that person of distinguished service to the State, etc. and is confirmed by the family relations register to have any of the following relationships with that person (for acquisition tax, limited to cases where they are confirmed to belong to the same household on the date of registration of the motor vehicle): <Amended on January 15, 2020>
1. The spouse, a lineal relative by blood, or a sibling of the person of distinguished service to the State, etc.;
2. The spouse of a lineal relative by blood of the person of distinguished service to the State, etc.;
3. A lineal relative by blood or a sibling of the spouse of the person of distinguished service to the State, etc.
(4) In applying paragraph (3), where both the person of distinguished service to the State, etc. and the person falling under any subparagraph of that paragraph have registered as foreigners under Article 31 of the Immigration Act and have permanent resident status under Article 10-3 of that Act, the registered foreigner records, etc. may substitute for the family relations register and the household resident registration record. <Added on January 15, 2020>
(5) Replacement acquisition under the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 29 (4) of the Act means a case where a motor vehicle exempted from acquisition tax or automobile tax under Article 29 of the Act is deregistered or its transfer is registered (meaning transfer to a person other than the person in whose name it was jointly registered with the person of distinguished service to the State, etc.; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph), and another motor vehicle is acquired (including a case where, within 60 days from the date of acquisition and registration of the other vehicle, the former vehicle exempted from acquisition tax or automobile tax is deregistered or its transfer is registered). <Amended on December 31, 2018; January 15, 2020>
(6) Where a motor vehicle owned by a person exempted from acquisition tax and automobile tax under Article 29 (4) of the Act falls under any of the following, the person shall be deemed not to own that motor vehicle from that date, regardless of whether it remains entered in the motor vehicle register: <Amended on December 30, 2016; January 15, 2020>
1. Where the person requests a motor vehicle dealer under the Motor Vehicle Management Act to arrange the sale of the motor vehicle: Provided, That where the motor vehicle is returned without being sold, the person shall be deemed to own it;
2. Where the head of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu recognizes that the motor vehicle is irretrievable or unusable because it has disappeared, been destroyed, or been damaged by a natural disaster, fire, traffic accident, etc.;
3. Where a motor vehicle dismantling and recycling business operator under the Motor Vehicle Management Act has scrapped the motor vehicle;
4. Where the motor vehicle has been exported after an export declaration has been filed with the head of a customs office under the Customs Act.

Article 13 (Scope of Rental Dormitories)
(1) "Portions prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as units with an exclusive use area of not more than 40 square meters" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 31 (1) of the Act means the following portions:
1. Units with an exclusive use area of not more than 40 square meters and their appurtenant land;
2. Of the portions used jointly by residents, such as living rooms, kitchens, bathrooms, corridors, and stairs, the portion corresponding to the ratio obtained by dividing the aggregate exclusive use area of units with an exclusive use area of not more than 40 square meters by the aggregate exclusive use area of all units, and the land appurtenant to that portion.
(2) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 31 (3) 2 of the Act means cases prescribed in Article 54 (2) 1 and 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Public Housing.
(3) "Housing and buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 31 (6) of the Act means the following:
1. Detached houses, multi-occupancy houses, and multi-family houses under subparagraph 1 (a) through (c) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act and their appurtenant land;
2. Apartments, row houses, and multi-household houses under subparagraph 2 (a) through (c) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act (limited to apartments, row houses, and multi-household houses not exceeding the national housing size under subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Housing Act) and their appurtenant land;
3. Dormitories under subparagraph 2 (d) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act (limited to those with an exclusive use area of not more than 85 square meters) and their appurtenant land;
4. Officetels under subparagraph 14 (b) (2) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act meeting all the following requirements, and their appurtenant land:
(a) The exclusive use area shall not exceed 85 square meters;
(b) They shall have a private kitchen with a standing work area equipped with water supply and sewerage facilities, a private flush toilet, and bathing facilities (including cases where bathing facilities are installed in the private flush toilet).

Article 13-2 (Scope of Multi-Family Houses)
(1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the items of Article 31-3 (3) 2 of the Act means cases prescribed in Article 43 (4) of the Special Act on Private Rental Housing. <Amended on December 31, 2024>
(2) "Multi-family house prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 31-3 (4) of the Act means a multi-family house (for a multi-family house only part of which is rented out under Article 2-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Private Rental Housing, limited to the portion provided for rental purposes) whose exclusive use area is separately entered for each unit in the building register under Article 38 of the Building Act. <Amended on December 31, 2024>
(3) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 31-3 (5) of the Act means cases where registration as a rental business operator has been cancelled on grounds under Article 43 (4) of the Special Act on Private Rental Housing. <Added on January 15, 2020; December 31, 2024>

Article 13-3 (Scope of Housing and Buildings Intended for Rental by Public Housing Project Operators)
"Housing and buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 31-5 (1) of the Act means those specified in the subparagraphs of Article 13 (3).

Article 14 (Scope of Small Multi-Unit Housing)
(1) Real estate for small multi-unit housing under Article 32 (1) of the Act means multi-unit housing with a building area (meaning exclusive use area) of not more than 60 square meters per unit (meaning a portion partitioned for independent and separate use by one household; hereinafter the same shall apply) (including ancillary facilities jointly used by residents of the multi-unit housing, land used for public purposes, and welfare facilities within permanent rental housing complexes whose entire rental income is used to meet rental housing management expenses), and its appurtenant land (including land for public facilities to vest in the State or a local government without compensation under relevant statutes).
(2) "Period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 32 (3) of the Act means four years from the date of acquisition of land for small multi-unit housing under paragraph (1) (meaning the final acquisition date if the land is not acquired all at once, or the date of approval of the project plan if the project plan is approved before the final acquisition date).

Article 15 (Scope of Housing Construction Business Operators)
(1) "Housing construction business operator prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33 (1) of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended on June 28, 2013; August 11, 2016>
1. A person who, before the date on which the certificate of approval for use of the relevant building is issued, has been issued a business registration certificate for construction business or real estate sales business under Article 8 of the Value-Added Tax Act, or has been assigned a unique identification number under Article 8 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act;
2. An employer under Article 4 (1) 6 of the Housing Act.
(2) "Housing for ordinary people prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33 (2) of the Act means housing with a gross floor area or exclusive use area of not more than 40 square meters [meaning a residential building and its appurtenant land that constitute housing under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Housing Act and are entered as housing in a building register, certificate of approval for use, or certificate of temporary approval for use under the Building Act, or in a register under the Registration of Real Estate Act {housing that could be constructed without a building permit or building report under the Building Act (meaning that Act before amendment by Act No. 7696) (including cases deemed to have obtained a building permit or filed a building report under Article 3 of the Addenda to the Act Partially Amending the Building Act, Act No. 7696), but is not entered in the building register, shall also be deemed to be entered as housing in the building register}; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article], with an acquisition value of less than 100 million won. <Amended on January 15, 2020>
(3) "One house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33 (2) of the Act means that, as of the acquisition date, one household consisting of family members entered in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer (excluding cohabitants) owns one house in the Republic of Korea (the acquirer's spouse, the acquirer's unmarried lineal descendants under 30 years of age, or the parents of the acquirer where the acquirer is unmarried and under 30 years of age shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not entered in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer); ownership of only the land appurtenant to a house shall also be deemed ownership of a house. In such cases, a person supporting a lineal ascendant aged 65 or older, a lineal ascendant who is a person of distinguished service to the State under the Act on the Honorable Treatment of and Support for Persons of Distinguished Service to the State (limited to a person assessed as having a disability of Grade 1 through 7), or a lineal ascendant registered as a person with a disability under the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities (limited to a person with a severe disability) shall be deemed not to belong to the same household as that ascendant even if they are entered in the same household resident registration record. <Amended on December 30, 2016; December 31, 2018>

Article 16 (Scope of One House per Household for Housing Eligible for Housing-Backed Retirement Pension Guarantees)
(1) "One house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 35 (1) 1 of the Act means that, as of the tax base date, one household consisting of family members entered in the same household resident registration record as the house owner (excluding cohabitants) owns one house in the Republic of Korea (the owner's spouse and unmarried lineal descendants under 30 years of age shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not entered in the same household resident registration record as the owner); ownership of only the land appurtenant to a house shall also be deemed ownership of a house. <Amended on January 15, 2020>
(2) In applying paragraph (1), where a house owned in addition to the house provided as security for a housing-backed retirement pension guarantee falls under any of the following, that house shall be deemed not to be owned: <Amended on December 31, 2019; May 26, 2020; May 7, 2024; September 10, 2024>
1. A house constructed outside an urban area under Article 6 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (meaning an urban area as of the tax base date), or in the administrative area of a Myeon (excluding the Seoul Metropolitan Area), which falls under any of the following:
(a) A detached house under subparagraph 1 (a) of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act (hereinafter referred to as a "detached house") for which at least 20 years have elapsed since approval for use;
(b) A detached house of not more than 85 square meters;
(c) A house acquired by inheritance;
2. A house with an exclusive use area of not more than 20 square meters: Provided, That cases where two or more houses with an exclusive use area of not more than 20 square meters are owned shall be excluded;
3. Designated cultural heritage under the Act on the Preservation and Utilization of Cultural Heritage, nationally registered cultural heritage under the Act on the Preservation and Utilization of Modern and Contemporary Cultural Heritage, or natural monuments, etc. under the Act on the Preservation and Utilization of Natural Heritage.

Article 17 (Scope of Public Interest Corporations)
"Corporation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 36 of the Act means Habitat for Humanity Korea, an incorporated association to which Article 4 (1) 4 of the Housing Act applies. <Amended on August 11, 2016; December 31, 2024>

Article 17-2 (Scope of Housing Eligible for Acquisition Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Newlywed Couples Purchasing Their First Home)
(1) "Cases where a person has owned or owns housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 36-2 (1) 1 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where a person owned a co-ownership share in a house by inheritance (including cases where only a co-ownership share in the land appurtenant to a house was owned) and has disposed of the entire share;
2. Where a person who owned a house falling under any of the following, constructed outside an urban area under Article 6 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (meaning an urban area as of the acquisition date), or in the administrative area of a Myeon (excluding the Seoul Metropolitan Area), resided in the area in which the house is located and then moved to another area (meaning an area outside the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province, Si, or Gun in which the house is located). In such cases, this shall be limited to cases where the house was disposed of before the acquisition date of the house eligible for reduction or exemption, or within three months from that acquisition date:
(a) A detached house for which at least 20 years have elapsed since approval for use;
(b) A detached house of not more than 85 square meters;
(c) A house acquired by inheritance;
3. Where a person owns or has disposed of a house with an exclusive use area of not more than 20 square meters: Provided, That cases where the person has owned or owns two or more houses with an exclusive use area of not more than 20 square meters shall be excluded;
4. Where a person owns or has disposed of a house whose standard market value calculated under Article 4 (2) of the Local Tax Act is not more than one million won as of the acquisition date.
(2) "One house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 36-2 (2) 2 of the Act means that one household consisting of family members entered in the same household resident registration record as the house acquirer (excluding cohabitants) owns one house in the Republic of Korea (the acquirer's spouse and unmarried lineal descendants under 30 years of age shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not entered in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer); ownership of only the land appurtenant to a house shall also be deemed ownership of a house.

Article 17-3 Deleted. <December 31, 2025>

Article 17-4 (Requirements for Housing Acquisition Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Childbirth and Child-Raising)
(1) "One house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 36-5 (1) 2 of the Act means that one household consisting of family members entered in the same household resident registration record as the house acquirer (excluding cohabitants) owns one house in the Republic of Korea (the acquirer's spouse and unmarried lineal descendants under 30 years of age shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not entered in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer). In such cases, ownership of only the land appurtenant to a house shall also be deemed ownership of a house.
(2) Deleted. <December 31, 2025>

Article 17-5 (Scope of Temporary Ownership of Two Houses Eligible for Acquisition Tax Reductions or Exemptions)
"Cases of temporary ownership of two houses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 40-2 2 of the Act means cases where another house has been acquired due to relocation, a change of workplace, schooling of the person or a family member, medical treatment for illness, or other grounds, but the former house has not yet been disposed of.

SECTION 3 SUPPORT FOR EDUCATION, SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY, ETC.

Article 18 (Scope of Businesses of Schools Eligible for Exemption)
(1) "Dormitory prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 41 (1) of the Act means a dormitory under Article 18-2. <Added on December 29, 2017>
(2) "Appurtenant land of a building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 41 (2) of the Act means appurtenant land of a building to be directly used for the relevant business where the building is under construction, or appurtenant land of a planned building where construction cannot commence after a building permit has been granted because of building restrictions imposed by an administrative agency. <Amended on December 29, 2017>
(3) "License for direct use by a school, etc. for its business" in the main clause of Article 41 (3) of the Act means a license necessary for a school, etc. under Article 41 (1) of the Act to operate its nonprofit business, or a license where all proceeds arising from the business facilities or activities authorized by that license are used for its nonprofit business. <Amended on December 29, 2017>
(4) "Business place portion and employee portion of resident tax prescribed by Presidential Decree in connection with profit-making business" in the proviso to Article 41 (3) of the Act means the business place portion (limited to the amount imposed under Article 81 (1) 2 of the Local Tax Act) and the employee portion of resident tax imposed on the basis of the business places and employees used for profit-making business. In such cases, where a building is used both for a business eligible for exemption and for a profit-making business, or an employee concurrently performs duties for both, the principal use or duty shall govern. <Amended on March 14, 2014; December 29, 2017; December 31, 2020>
(5) "Basic property for profit-making purposes prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 41 (8) of the Act means basic property for profit-making purposes under Article 7 (1) of the Regulations on the Establishment and Operation of Universities and Colleges. <Added on December 29, 2023>

Article 18-2 (Scope of Dormitories Established and Operated as Private Investment Projects Eligible for Exemption)
"Dormitory prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 42 (1) of the Act means a dormitory established and operated by any of the following methods:
1. A method whereby a project operator constructing a dormitory used by a school, etc. under Article 42 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "school, etc." in this Article) (hereinafter referred to as a "project operator" in this Article) is granted ownership of the facility after completion for a period specified in an agreement with the school, etc., and ownership of the facility vests in the school, etc. upon expiry of that period;
2. A method whereby ownership of the facility vests in the school, etc. upon completion and the project operator is granted the right to manage and operate the facility for a period specified in an agreement with the school, etc. (excluding cases falling under subparagraph 3);
3. A method whereby ownership of the facility vests in the school, etc. upon completion and the project operator is granted the right to manage and operate the facility for a period specified in an agreement with the school, etc., while the facility is leased for use and enjoyment of its benefits for the period specified in the agreement.

Article 19 (Scope of Businesses of Industry-Academic Cooperation Foundations Eligible for Exemption)
"Business place portion and employee portion of resident tax prescribed by Presidential Decree in connection with profit-making business" in the proviso to Article 42 (4) of the Act means the business place portion (limited to the amount imposed under Article 81 (1) 2 of the Local Tax Act) and the employee portion of resident tax imposed on the basis of the business places and employees used for profit-making business. In such cases, where a building is used both for a business eligible for exemption and for a profit-making business, or an employee concurrently performs duties for both, the principal use or duty shall govern. <Amended on March 14, 2014; December 31, 2020>

Article 20 (Scope of Businesses of Lifelong Education Organizations Eligible for Exemption)
(1) "Appurtenant land of a building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 43 (2) of the Act and in the part other than the subparagraphs of paragraph (3) of that Article respectively means appurtenant land of a building to be directly used for the relevant business where the building is under construction, or appurtenant land of a planned building where construction cannot commence after a building permit has been granted because of building restrictions imposed by an administrative agency. <Amended on December 31, 2018>
(2) Deleted. <December 31, 2018>
(3) Deleted. <December 31, 2018>

Article 21 (Scope of Lifelong Education Facilities)
"Lifelong education facility prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 44 (1) of the Act means any of the following lifelong education facilities that have been reported, authorized, registered, or notified under the Lifelong Education Act: <Amended on April 22, 2013; December 31, 2015; December 31, 2018>
1. A school-affiliated lifelong education facility under Article 30 of the Lifelong Education Act;
2. A school-type lifelong education facility under Article 31 of the Lifelong Education Act;
3. An in-house university-type lifelong education facility under Article 32 of the Lifelong Education Act;
4. A distance university-type lifelong education facility under Article 33 of the Lifelong Education Act;
5. A workplace-affiliated lifelong education facility under Article 35 of the Lifelong Education Act;
6. A civil society organization-affiliated lifelong education facility under Article 36 of the Lifelong Education Act;
7. A media organization-affiliated lifelong education facility under Article 37 of the Lifelong Education Act;
8. A lifelong education facility related to knowledge and human resources development business under Article 38 of the Lifelong Education Act.

Article 21-2 (Scope of Museums)
(1) "Museum or art museum prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 44-2 (1) of the Act means a museum or art museum registered under Article 16 of the Museum and Art Gallery Support Act.
(2) "Library or science museum prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 44-2 (2) of the Act means the following libraries or science museums: <Amended on December 6, 2022>
1. A public library registered under Article 36 of the Libraries Act [until December 31, 2024, including a special library registered under Article 40 of the former Libraries Act (meaning that Act before amendment by Act No. 18547)];
2. A science museum registered under Article 6 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Science Museums.
(3) "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as cancellation of registration under relevant statutes" in Article 44-2 (3) 3 of the Act means any of the following cases: <Added on December 31, 2024>
1. Where closure has been reported under Article 22 of the Museum and Art Gallery Support Act or registration has been cancelled under Article 29 of that Act;
2. Where closure has been reported under Article 36 (5) of the Libraries Act or registration has been cancelled under Article 38 of that Act;
3. Where registration has been cancelled under Article 12 of the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Science Museums or closure has been notified under Article 14 of that Act.

Article 22 (Definition of Academic Organizations)
(1) "Academic organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 45 (1) of the Act means a corporation or organization whose purpose is academic research, presentation activities, etc. under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Academic Promotion Act and which falls under any of the following: Provided, That a public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions shall be excluded: <Amended on December 29, 2023>
1. A public interest corporation established under Article 4 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Public Interest Corporations;
2. A nonprofit corporation established under Article 32 of the Civil Act;
3. A corporation established under statutes other than the Civil Act and the Commercial Act;
4. A nonprofit nongovernmental organization registered under Article 4 of the Assistance for Non-Profit, Non-Governmental Organizations Act.
(2) "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as revocation of permission for establishment under relevant statutes" in Article 45 (3) 3 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where permission for establishment of a public interest corporation has been revoked under Article 16 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Public Interest Corporations;
2. Where permission for establishment of a nonprofit corporation has been revoked under Article 38 of the Civil Act;
3. Where registration of a nonprofit nongovernmental organization has been cancelled under Article 4-2 of the Assistance for Non-Profit, Non-Governmental Organizations Act.

Article 23 (Corporate-Affiliated Research Institutes)
(1) "Corporate-affiliated research institute prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 46 (1) of the Act means a corporate-affiliated research institute recognized under Article 7 (1) of the Act on Support for Research and Development of Corporate-Affiliated Research Institutes, Etc. <Amended on January 27, 2026>
(2) "Corporate-affiliated research institute for research in new growth and original technology fields prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 46 (2) 1 of the Act means a corporate-affiliated research institute under paragraph (1) belonging to an enterprise that meets all the following requirements: <Amended on January 27, 2026>
1. It shall be an enterprise located in the Republic of Korea engaging in an industry under subparagraph 1 (a) or (b) of Article 2 of the Research Industry Promotion Act and performing new growth and original technology research and development activities under Article 9 (3) 1 (a) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (hereinafter referred to as "new growth and original technology research and development activities" in this subparagraph) (including cases where it performs both new growth and original technology research and development activities and other research and development);
2. It shall be an enterprise that, within three years from the date on which its research institute was recognized as a corporate-affiliated research institute under Article 7 (1) of the Act on Support for Research and Development of Corporate-Affiliated Research Institutes, Etc., has been notified by the Research and Development Tax Credit Technology Deliberation Committee under Article 9 (15) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act of a deliberation result that the technology subject to research and development by the relevant corporate-affiliated research institute falls under the technologies specified in attached Table 7 of that Decree.
(3) "Corporate-affiliated research institute for research in national strategic technology fields prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 46 (2) 2 of the Act means a corporate-affiliated research institute under paragraph (1) belonging to an enterprise that meets all the following requirements:
1. It shall be an enterprise located in the Republic of Korea engaging in an industry under subparagraph 1 (a) or (b) of Article 2 of the Research Industry Promotion Act and performing national strategic technology research and development activities under Article 9 (7) 1 (a) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (hereinafter referred to as "national strategic technology research and development activities" in this subparagraph) (including cases where it performs both national strategic technology research and development activities and other research and development);
2. It shall be an enterprise that, within three years from the date on which its research institute was recognized as a corporate-affiliated research institute under Article 7 (1) of the Act on Support for Research and Development of Corporate-Affiliated Research Institutes, Etc., has been notified by the Research and Development Tax Credit Technology Deliberation Committee under Article 9 (15) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act of a deliberation result that the technology subject to research and development by the relevant corporate-affiliated research institute falls under the technologies specified in attached Table 7-2 of that Decree.
(4) "Committee prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 46 (3) 2 of the Act means the Research and Development Tax Credit Technology Deliberation Committee under Article 9 (15) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
(5) "New growth and original technology or national strategic technology prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 46 (3) 2 of the Act means a technology specified in attached Table 7 or attached Table 7-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 24 (Reductions and Exemptions for Environment-Friendly Buildings)
(1) The acquisition tax reduction rates under the part other than the subparagraphs of Article 47-2 (1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on January 1, 2014; December 31, 2014; December 30, 2016; December 29, 2017; December 31, 2020; December 31, 2024>
1. A building with the highest green building certification grade certified under Article 16 of the Green Buildings Construction Support Act (hereinafter referred to as a "green building certification grade" in this Article): 10 percent;
(a) Deleted. <December 31, 2020>
(b) Deleted. <December 31, 2020>
2. A building with an excellent green building certification grade: Five percent.
(2) "At or above the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 47-2 (1) 1 of the Act means that the green building certification grade is excellent or higher. <Amended on January 1, 2014; December 31, 2014; December 30, 2016>
(3) Deleted. <December 31, 2024>
(4) The acquisition tax reduction rates under Article 47-2 (2) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended on December 31, 2020; December 31, 2024>
1. A building whose zero-energy building certification grade certified under Article 17 of the Green Buildings Construction Support Act (hereinafter referred to as a "zero-energy building certification grade" in this Article) is Plus or Grade 1 through 3: 20 percent;
2. A building with zero-energy building certification Grade 4: 18 percent;
3. A building with zero-energy building certification Grade 5: 15 percent.
(5) "Energy-saving environment-friendly housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 47-2 (3) of the Act means housing under Article 64 of the Regulations on Housing Construction Standards, Etc. (hereinafter referred to as "environment-friendly housing" in this Article) for which the authority conducting inspections for use under Article 49 of the Housing Act has confirmed that the total energy saving rate or total carbon dioxide reduction rate (hereinafter referred to as the "energy saving rate, etc." in this Article) is at least 65 percent. <Added on December 30, 2010; December 31, 2011; December 31, 2014; August 11, 2016; December 30, 2016; December 29, 2017; December 31, 2020>
(6) The property tax reduction rates under the main clause of Article 47-2 (5) of the Act shall be as follows: <Added on December 31, 2011; January 1, 2014; December 31, 2014; December 29, 2017>
1. Where the green building certification grade is the highest:
(a) Where the energy efficiency grade is Grade 1+ or higher: 10 percent;
(b) Where the energy efficiency grade is Grade 1: Seven percent;
(c) Deleted. <December 29, 2017>
2. Where the green building certification grade is excellent:
(a) Where the energy efficiency grade is Grade 1+ or higher: Seven percent;
(b) Where the energy efficiency grade is Grade 1: Three percent;
3. Deleted. <December 29, 2017>
(7) The amount of the property tax reduction for housing under Article 47-2 (6) of the Act shall be calculated according to the following formula: <Added on December 31, 2011; December 31, 2014; December 29, 2017>

Reduction amount = Calculated tax amount × [Standard market value of the building / (Standard market value of the building + Standard market value of the land)] × Reduction rate

Note: Calculated tax amount means the tax amount calculated for housing under subparagraph 3 of Article 104 of the Local Tax Act, including its appurtenant land.

(8) The acquisition tax reduction rates under Article 47-3 (1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Added on December 31, 2011; December 31, 2014; June 15, 2015>
1. A building whose new and renewable energy supply ratio (meaning the ratio of energy supplied using new energy and renewable energy under subparagraphs 1 and 2 of Article 2 of the Act on the Promotion of the Development, Use and Diffusion of New and Renewable Energy to the total energy consumption of the building; hereinafter the same shall apply in this paragraph) exceeds 20 percent: 15 percent;
2. A building whose new and renewable energy supply ratio is not more than 20 percent but exceeds 15 percent: 10 percent;
3. A building whose new and renewable energy supply ratio is not more than 15 percent but exceeds 10 percent: Five percent.

Article 24-2 (Reductions and Exemptions for Buildings Certified as Earthquake-Safe Facilities)
"Rate prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 47-4 (3) of the Act means five percent.

SECTION 4 SUPPORT FOR CULTURE, TOURISM, ETC.

Article 25 (Scope of Businesses of Organizations Established for Religious and Ritual Purposes Eligible for Exemption)
(1) "Appurtenant land of a building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 50 (2) of the Act means appurtenant land of a building to be directly used for the relevant business where the building is under construction, or appurtenant land of a planned building where construction cannot commence after a building permit has been granted because of building restrictions imposed by an administrative agency.
(2) "License for direct use by an organization under paragraph (1) for its business" in the main clause of Article 50 (3) of the Act means a license necessary for an organization established for religious and ritual purposes under Article 50 (1) of the Act to operate its nonprofit business, or a license where all proceeds arising from the business facilities or activities authorized by that license are used for its nonprofit business.
(3) "Business place portion and employee portion of resident tax prescribed by Presidential Decree in connection with profit-making business" in the proviso to Article 50 (3) of the Act means the business place portion (limited to the amount imposed under Article 81 (1) 2 of the Local Tax Act) and the employee portion of resident tax imposed on the basis of the business places and employees directly used for profit-making business. In such cases, where a building is used both for a business eligible for exemption and for a profit-making business, or an employee concurrently performs duties for both, the principal use or duty shall govern. <Amended on March 14, 2014; December 31, 2020>

Article 26 (Definition of Cultural and Arts Organizations and Sports Organizations)
(1) "Cultural and arts organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 52 (1) of the Act means a corporation or organization whose purpose is the creation and promotion of culture and arts under Article 2 (1) 1 of the Culture and Arts Promotion Act, etc., and which falls under any of the following: Provided, That a public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions shall be excluded: <Amended on December 29, 2023>
1. A public interest corporation established under Article 4 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Public Interest Corporations;
2. A nonprofit corporation established under Article 32 of the Civil Act;
3. A corporation established under statutes other than the Civil Act and the Commercial Act;
4. A nonprofit nongovernmental organization registered under Article 4 of the Assistance for Non-Profit, Non-Governmental Organizations Act.
(2) "Sports organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 52 (2) of the Act means a corporation or organization whose purpose is activities or business relating to sports under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the National Sports Promotion Act and which falls under any subparagraph of paragraph (1): Provided, That a public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions shall be excluded. <Amended on December 29, 2023>
(3) "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as revocation of permission for establishment under relevant statutes" in Article 52 (3) 3 of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Where permission for establishment of a public interest corporation has been revoked under Article 16 of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Public Interest Corporations;
2. Where permission for establishment of a nonprofit corporation has been revoked under Article 38 of the Civil Act;
3. Where registration of a nonprofit nongovernmental organization has been cancelled under Article 4-2 of the Assistance for Non-Profit, Non-Governmental Organizations Act.

Article 27 Deleted. <December 31, 2025>

