Article 28-2 (Scope of Corporate Mergers, etc.)
(1) "Merger prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 57-2 (1) of the Act means a merger between corporations that, as of the merger date, have continuously engaged for at least 1 year in a business other than a consumptive service business under Article 29 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (including cases where a consumptive service business is operated concurrently with another business and the revenue of the consumptive service business is the largest among the revenues by business line in the business year immediately preceding the business year in which the merger date falls; hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as a "consumptive service business") (hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as "merging corporations"). In such cases, a merger in which a corporation that has engaged in a consumptive service business for at least 1 year ceases to exist as a result of the merger and the merging corporation does not engage in a consumptive service business shall be included. <Amended 2024.12.31>
(2) "Corporation engaged in a technologically innovative business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 57-2 (1) of the Act means a corporation falling under any of the following: <Amended 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31, 2024.7.2, 2024.12.31, 2026.5.19>
1. A corporation confirmed as a venture business pursuant to Article 25 of the Special Act on the Promotion of Venture Businesses by the date of registration of the merger;
2. A corporation selected as a technologically innovative small and medium enterprise pursuant to Article 15 of the Act on the Promotion of Technology Innovation of Small and Medium Enterprises and Article 13 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act by the date of registration of the merger;
3. A small and medium enterprise whose research and human resources development expenses under the former part of Article 10 (1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, other than its subparagraphs, in the business year immediately preceding the business year in which the date of registration of the merger falls amount to at least 5/100 of its sales;
4. A small and medium enterprise that has obtained any of the following certifications, etc. by the date of registration of the merger:
(a) Certification of new health technology under Article 8 (1) of the Health and Medical Service Technology Promotion Act;
(b) Designation of new technology under Article 15-2 (1) of the Industrial Technology Innovation Promotion Act;
(c) Designation of a new product under Article 16 (1) of the Industrial Technology Innovation Promotion Act;
(d) Certification as an innovative pharmaceutical enterprise under Article 7 (2) of the Special Act on the Promotion of and Support for the Pharmaceutical Industry;
(e) Selection of middle-standing enterprises, etc. under Article 18 (1) of the Special Act on the Promotion of Growth and the Strengthening of Competitiveness of Middle-Standing Enterprises.
(3) "Justifiable grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 57-2 (4) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended 2018.12.31>
1. Where the relevant business property is expropriated pursuant to the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works or any other Act;
2. Where the relevant business is discontinued or business property is disposed of pursuant to an order to close or relocate the business, etc. under statutes or regulations;
3. Where any subparagraph of Article 29 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act applies;
4. Where less than 50/100 of the shares acquired through conversion into a corporation under Article 32 (1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act are disposed of.
(4) Deleted <2024.12.31>
(5) Deleted <2016.12.30>
(6) "Where a division is carried out as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 57-2 (9) of the Act means a case where the National Federation of Fisheries Cooperatives under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Fisheries Cooperatives Act separates its credit business and establishes Suhyup Bank pursuant to Article 141-4 (1) of that Act. <Added 2016.11.30>
(7) "Subsidiary newly established through a division as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 57-2 (9) 1 of the Act means Suhyup Bank established pursuant to Article 141-4 (1) of the Fisheries Cooperatives Act. <Added 2016.11.30>

Article 28-3 (Requirements for Purchase and Lease of Assets by the Korea Asset Management Corporation)
"Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 57-3 (5) of the Act means satisfying all of the following requirements: <Amended 2021.12.31>
1. Receiving from the relevant small and medium enterprise a financial structure improvement plan containing details of its debts to financial companies and a repayment plan;
2. Entering into a lease agreement under which the relevant small and medium enterprise continues to use its assets when those assets are purchased from it.

Article 29 (Scope of Industrial Buildings, etc.)
(1) "Buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the introductory part of Article 58 (3) of the Act means buildings falling under any of the following: <Amended 2017.12.29, 2023.3.14, 2024.7.2>
1. Buildings for gas supply facilities under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Urban Gas Business Act [in the case of pipeline facilities under Article 5 (1) 4 of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act (including connecting facilities; hereinafter the same shall apply) installed in new technology startup cluster areas under the Special Act on the Promotion of Venture Businesses, limited to pipeline facilities for supplying gas to the relevant areas];
