(2) "Real estate for factories prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the introductory part of Article 58 (3) of the Act means factories under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act. <Added 2017.12.29>

Article 29-2 (Scope of Startup Small and Medium Enterprises, etc.)
(1) "Date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of the introductory part of Article 58-3 (1) of the Act means a date falling under any of the following: <Added 2016.12.30>
1. Where a corporation starts a business: The date of registration of incorporation;
2. Where an individual starts a business: The date of business registration under Article 8 of the Value-Added Tax Act.
(2) "Youth startup enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 58-3 (1) of the Act means a startup small and medium enterprise under the introductory part of that paragraph whose representative (in the case of a joint place of business under Article 43 (1) of the Income Tax Act, meaning the business operator with the larger profit and loss sharing ratio under paragraph (2) of that Article; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) satisfies the requirements specified in the following subparagraphs: <Added 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31>
1. Where a business is started as an individual business operator: A person aged at least 15 and not more than 34 at the time of starting the business: Provided, That, where the person has performed military service falling under any item of Article 27 (1) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, a person whose age, calculated by subtracting the period of that service (up to a maximum of 6 years) from his or her age at the time of starting the business, is not more than 34 shall be included;
2. Where a business is started as a corporation: A person satisfying all of the following requirements:
(a) Satisfying the requirements of subparagraph 1;
(b) Being a controlling shareholder, etc. under Article 43 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act who is the largest shareholder or largest equity investor in the relevant corporation.
(3) "Standard factory site area prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 58-3 (1) 2 and (2) 2 of the Act means, respectively, the standard factory site area under Article 102 (1) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act, and "applicable multiplier for each land-use zone prescribed by Presidential Decree" means, respectively, the applicable multiplier for each land-use zone under Article 101 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act. <Amended 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31>
(4) "Enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 58-3 (2) of the Act means an enterprise falling under any of the following: <Amended 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31, 2024.7.2>
1. A small and medium enterprise satisfying the requirements of Article 2-2 of the Special Act on the Promotion of Venture Businesses (excluding a small and medium enterprise falling under paragraph (1) 2 (b) of that Article);
2. A small and medium enterprise whose research and development and human resources development expenses specified in Attached Table 6 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act amount to at least 5/100 of its revenue for the relevant taxable year (limited to cases where the ratio of research and development and human resources development expenses has been maintained at 5/100 or more from the taxable year in which the date of confirmation of its status as a venture business pursuant to Article 25 of the Special Act on the Promotion of Venture Businesses falls).
(5) "Youth startup venture enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 58-3 (2) of the Act means a startup venture small and medium enterprise under the introductory part of that paragraph whose representative satisfies the requirements of the subparagraphs of paragraph (2). <Added 2020.12.31>
(6) "Engineering business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 58-3 (4) 5 of the Act means a business providing engineering activities under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Engineering Industry Promotion Act, where a report as an engineering business operator has been filed pursuant to Article 21 of that Act or registration as a professional engineer (including renewal of registration) has been completed pursuant to Article 5-7 of the Professional Engineers Act. <Added 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.1.15, 2020.12.31, 2024.12.31>
(7) "Logistics industry prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 58-3 (4) 9 of the Act means the logistics industry under Article 5 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Added 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31>
(8) "Tourist facility business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 58-3 (4) 11 of the Act means specialized resort businesses and comprehensive resort businesses under Article 2 (1) 3 (a) and (b) of the Enforcement Decree of the Tourism Promotion Act. <Added 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31>
(9) "Business assets prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as land, buildings, and machinery and equipment" in the proviso to Article 58-3 (6) 1 of the Act means land and depreciable assets under Article 24 of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act. <Added 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31>
(10) "Ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 58-3 (6) 1 of the Act means 30/100. <Added 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31>
(11) Businesses of the same type under Article 58-3 (6) 1 and 3 of the Act shall be businesses falling within the same class under the standard classification of industries publicly notified by the head of the National Data Office pursuant to Article 22 of the Statistics Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korean Standard Industrial Classification"). <Added 2016.12.30, 2018.12.31, 2020.12.31, 2025.10.1>
(12) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 58-3 (6) 5 of the Act means any of the following cases: <Added 2023.12.29>
1. Where an individual business operator newly establishes a small and medium enterprise that is a corporation engaging in the same type of business and becomes an oligopolistic shareholder (meaning an oligopolistic shareholder under subparagraph 2 of Article 46 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article);
2. Where the relevant corporation or an oligopolistic shareholder of that corporation becomes an oligopolistic shareholder of a newly established small and medium enterprise that is a corporation (limited to cases where the relevant corporation and the newly established small and medium enterprise that is a corporation engage in the same type of business);
3. Where a small and medium enterprise that is a corporation continues to engage in the same type of business as before a change in its corporate form after making that change.

Article 29-3 (Scope of Cooperatives and Business Cooperatives Eligible for Acquisition Tax Reduction)
"Cooperatives and business cooperatives established with business operators prescribed by Presidential Decree as members" in the proviso to Article 60 (1) of the Act means cooperatives and business cooperatives established with, as members, operators of supermarkets or other general retail businesses primarily selling food and beverages under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification. <Amended 2016.12.30>

Article 29-4 (Reductions or Exemptions for Projects to Foster Local Small and Medium Enterprises, etc.)
"Corporation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 60 (4) of the Act means a comprehensive support center for local small and medium enterprises under Article 20 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Fostering Local Small and Medium Enterprises and Promoting Innovation. <Amended 2016.9.29, 2022.1.25>

Article 29-5 (Conditions for Gas Stations Eligible for Property Tax Reduction)
"Where the conditions prescribed by Presidential Decree are satisfied" in Article 62-2 of the Act means a case where all of the following conditions are satisfied:
1. Being required to purchase at least 50 percent of the petroleum products sold from the Korea National Oil Corporation under the Korea National Oil Corporation Act;
2. Operating under the Altteul Gas Station brand.

Article 29-6 (Local Government Investment Ratio in Urban Railroad Corporations)
"Local government investment ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 63 (5) 1 of the Act means the ratio of the amount invested by a local government (where two or more local governments have jointly established the corporation, the sum of the amounts invested by each local government) to the capital of a local public corporation under Article 49 of the Local Public Enterprises Act established for the purpose of conducting urban railroad business under subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the Urban Railroad Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as an "urban railroad corporation"): Provided, That, where an urban railroad corporation has issued shares pursuant to Article 53 (3) of the Local Public Enterprises Act, it means the ratio of the number of shares owned by a local government (including shares deemed to have been contributed by the local government under paragraph (4) of that Article) (where two or more local governments own shares, the sum of the numbers of shares owned by each local government) to the total number of shares so issued.

SECTION 6 SUPPORT FOR TRANSPORTATION AND TRAFFIC

Article 30 (Scope of Ships for Cargo Transportation, etc.)
(1) "Ships for passenger and cargo transportation prescribed by Presidential Decree acquired for operation on coastal routes and ships for operation on foreign routes prescribed by Presidential Decree acquired for operation exclusively on foreign routes" in the main clause of the introductory part of Article 64 (2) of the Act means ships falling under any of the following: <Amended 2011.12.31, 2024.12.31>
1. Ships for coastal passenger and cargo transportation acquired by a person who has obtained a license for coastal passenger transportation business pursuant to Article 4 of the Marine Transportation Act or registered coastal cargo transportation business pursuant to Article 24 of that Act (including a person who obtains such a license or registers such business within 30 days from the date of acquisition), or by a person who has registered ship leasing business pursuant to Article 33 of that Act (including a person who registers ship leasing business within 30 days from the date of acquisition and a person who leases ships as a facilities leasing business operator under the Specialized Credit Finance Business Act; hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as a "person who has registered ship leasing business");
2. Ships falling under any of the following items that are not registered pursuant to the International Ship Registration Act:
(a) Ships used exclusively on foreign routes by a person who has obtained a license for oceangoing passenger transportation business pursuant to Article 4 of the Marine Transportation Act or registered oceangoing cargo transportation business pursuant to Article 24 of that Act (including a person who obtains such a license or registers such business within 30 days from the date of acquisition);
(b) Ships leased by a person who has registered ship leasing business on the condition that they be used exclusively on foreign routes;
(c) Distant water fishing vessels (including cases where a permit is obtained pursuant to Article 6 of the Distant Water Fisheries Development Act within 3 months from the date of acquisition).
(2) "Ships for cargo transportation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 64 (3) of the Act means ships under paragraph (1) 1. <Added 2016.12.30>

Article 30-2 (Criteria for Exclusion from Special Taxation for Air Transportation Business, etc.)
"Persons with an amount not less than the amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 65 of the Act means corporations required to submit annual business reports pursuant to Article 159 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act whose total assets on the statement of financial position for the immediately preceding business year (in the case of a newly established company without a statement of financial position for the immediately preceding business year, its paid-in capital at the time the tax liability arises under Article 34 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes) amount to at least 5 trillion won in aggregate.

Article 31 (Classification of Passenger Motor Vehicles for Non-Business Use, etc.)
(1) "Motor vehicles of the size prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 67 (1) and (2) of the Act means, respectively, passenger motor vehicles, vans, and trucks with an engine displacement of less than 1,000 cubic centimeters and measuring not more than 3.6 meters in length, 1.6 meters in width, and 2.0 meters in height: Provided, That only the length, width, and height criteria shall apply to motor vehicles using only electricity as their power source.
(2) "Passenger motor vehicles for non-business use prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 67 (1) of the Act means passenger motor vehicles used for non-business purposes under Article 122 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act. <Amended 2018.12.31>

Article 32 Deleted <2018.12.31>

Article 33 (Scope of Logistics Business, etc.)
(1) "Logistics business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 71 (2) of the Act means logistics business under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Framework Act on Logistics Policies. <Amended 2025.12.31>
(2) "Real estate for logistics facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 71 (2) of the Act means land acquired from an implementer of a logistics complex development project under Article 27 of the Act on the Development and Operation of Logistics Facilities to install general logistics complex facilities under subparagraph 7 of Article 2 of that Act (excluding large-scale stores under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Distribution Industry Development Act), and buildings acquired by newly constructing or extending them on that land within 5 years from the date of acquisition of the land (including buildings newly constructed or extended before the date of acquisition of the land). <Amended 2025.12.31>

SECTION 7 SUPPORT FOR NATIONAL LAND AND REGIONAL DEVELOPMENT

Article 34 (Standards for Calculating Excess Amounts upon Expropriation)
(1) The standards and methods for calculating excess amounts under the proviso to the introductory part of Article 73 (1) of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended 2018.12.31, 2021.12.31>
1. The excess amount where the replacement acquisition of real estate, etc. under the main clause of the introductory part of Article 73 (1) of the Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "real estate, etc.") falls under any of the following items: The amount obtained by subtracting the compensation for the real estate, etc. purchased, expropriated, or demolished from the actual acquisition price of the real estate, etc. acquired as a replacement;
(a) Acquisition from the State, a local government, or an association of local governments under Article 176 (1) of the Local Autonomy Act;
(b) Acquisition by importation from a foreign country;
(c) Acquisition for which the acquisition price is proved by corporate books, such as general ledgers, subsidiary ledgers, receipts and disbursement vouchers, and financial statements prepared by a corporation on the basis of objective documentary evidence, such as final judgments in civil or administrative litigation (excluding those based on settlement, waiver, admission of a claim, or deemed confession), financial transaction records of financial companies, or appraisal reports under Article 6 of the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers [where the acquisition price of a used motor vehicle or used machinery and equipment stated in corporate books is lower than the standard market price prescribed in Article 4 (2) of the Local Tax Act, the portion stating that acquisition price (excluding cases where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu recognizes that the value of the used motor vehicle or used machinery and equipment has fallen below the standard market price due to a natural disaster, fire, traffic accident, etc.) shall be excluded from corporate books in which the acquisition price is proved by objective documentary evidence];
(d) Acquisition by public sale;
(e) Acquisition for which verification has been conducted pursuant to Article 5 of the Act on Report on Real Estate Transactions, etc. after submission of a report under Article 3 of that Act;
2. The excess amount where the replacement acquisition of real estate, etc. is an acquisition other than those under the items of subparagraph 1: The amount obtained by subtracting the compensation for the real estate, etc. purchased, expropriated, or demolished at the time of such purchase, expropriation, or demolition from the acquisition tax base of the real estate, etc. acquired as a replacement (meaning the tax base under Articles 10-2 through 10-6 of the Local Tax Act).
(2) "Absentee real estate owner prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 73 (2) of the Act means a resident or business operator (including a corporation) who owns real estate to be purchased, expropriated, or demolished within a publicly notified project district under the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works or other relevant statutes or regulations and who, as of the contract date (limited to contracts concluded before the date of public notice of project approval) or the date of public notice of project approval, has not maintained resident registration or business registration continuously for the preceding 1 year in an area specified in the following subparagraphs, or who, despite having maintained resident registration or business registration continuously for the preceding 1 year, does not actually reside or conduct business there. In such cases, where real estate has been acquired by inheritance, the combined period of residence of the heir and the decedent shall be deemed the heir's period of residence. <Amended 2017.12.29, 2020.12.31>
1. Where the real estate purchased or expropriated is farmland: The Si/Gun/Gu in which it is located and adjoining Sis/Guns/Gus, or areas within 30 kilometers of the location of the farmland;
2. Where the real estate purchased, expropriated, or demolished is not farmland: The Gu [including a Gu that is not an autonomous Gu, and, in the case of a Si in the urban-rural integrated form, limited to Dong areas; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph], Si (meaning a Si without Gus that are not autonomous Gus, and, in the case of a Si in the urban-rural integrated form, limited to Dong areas; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph), Eup, or Myeon in which it is located and adjoining Gu, Si, Eup, or Myeon areas.

Article 35 (Standards for Calculating Excess Amounts of Real Estate Acquired under Land Substitution Plans, etc.)
(1) Deleted <2023.3.14>
(2) Deleted <2023.3.14>
(3) "Temporary owner of 2 houses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the introductory part of Article 74 (5) of the Act means a person who, as of the date of acquisition, owns 2 houses, including a house acquired through implementation of a redevelopment project under subparagraph 3 of that paragraph. In such cases, a person who owns only land attached to a house shall also be deemed to own a house, but a person who owns a co-ownership share in a house through inheritance (including a person who owns only a co-ownership share in land attached to a house) shall not be deemed to own a house. <Added 2020.1.15>
(4) "One house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the introductory part of Article 74 (5) of the Act and the introductory part of subparagraph 3 of that paragraph means, respectively, a case where a household composed of family members entered on the same household resident registration record as the acquirer of a house (excluding cohabitants) (the acquirer's spouse and unmarried lineal descendants under the age of 30 shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not entered on the same household resident registration record as the acquirer) owns 1 house in the Republic of Korea and that house has been acquired through implementation of a redevelopment project under subparagraph 2 (b) of Article 2 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments. In such cases, a person who owns only land attached to a house shall also be deemed to own a house. <Added 2020.1.15>
(5) "Cases of temporary ownership of 2 houses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 74 (5) 3 of the Act means cases falling under paragraph (3). <Added 2020.1.15>

Article 35-2 (Standards for Calculating Excess Amounts of Buildings Acquired as Compensation in Kind, etc.)
(1) The excess amount under the proviso to Article 74-2 (1) of the Act shall be calculated as specified in the following subparagraphs: <Amended 2025.7.31>
1. In the case of a building acquired as compensation in kind under Article 40-10 (5) or (7) of the Special Act on Public Housing (including land attached to the building; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph and subparagraph 2): The amount obtained by subtracting the amount for which payment was withheld from the sale price of the building provided as compensation in kind pursuant to the former part of Article 35-9 (10) of the Enforcement Decree of that Act;
2. In the case of a building acquired as compensation in kind under Article 55-3 (1) of the Special Act on the Promotion of and Support for Urban Regeneration: The amount obtained by subtracting the amount for which payment was withheld from the sale price of the building provided as compensation in kind pursuant to the former part of Article 53-5 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of that Act.
(2) "Temporary owner of 2 houses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the introductory part of Article 74-2 (3) of the Act means a temporary owner of 2 houses under Article 35 (3). In such cases, "redevelopment project under subparagraph 3 of that paragraph" in the former part of Article 35 (3) shall be construed as "complex projects and residential innovation district regeneration projects under Article 74-2 (3) of the Act."
(3) "Owner of one house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to the introductory part of Article 74-2 (3) of the Act means a person who owns one house per household under Article 35 (4). In such cases, "redevelopment project under subparagraph 2 (b) of Article 2 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments" in the former part of Article 35 (4) shall be construed as "complex projects and residential innovation district regeneration projects under Article 74-2 (3) of the Act."
(4) "Owner of one house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 74-2 (3) 3 of the Act means a person who owns one house per household under Article 35 (4). In such cases, "redevelopment project under subparagraph 2 (b) of Article 2 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments" in the former part of Article 35 (4) shall be construed as "complex projects and residential innovation district regeneration projects under Article 74-2 (3) of the Act."
(5) "Temporary owner of 2 houses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 74-2 (3) 3 of the Act means a temporary owner of 2 houses under Article 35 (3). In such cases, "redevelopment project under subparagraph 3 of that paragraph" in the former part of Article 35 (3) shall be construed as "complex projects and residential innovation district regeneration projects under Article 74-2 (3) of the Act."

Article 35-3 (Startup Enterprises, etc. within Enterprise Cities and Regional Development Project Districts)
(1) "Standards prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the introductory part of Article 75-2 (1) of the Act means the standards specified in the following subparagraphs: <Amended 2020.1.15>
1. Businesses eligible for reduction or exemption of acquisition tax or property tax pursuant to Article 75-2 (1) 1 and 3 of the Act: A business falling under any of the following items;
(a) A business falling under Article 116-2 (17) 1, 4, or 5 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act with an investment of at least 2 billion won and at least 30 regular employees;
(b) A business falling under Article 116-2 (17) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act with an investment of at least 500 million won and at least 10 regular employees;
(c) A business falling under Article 116-2 (17) 3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act with an investment of at least 1 billion won and at least 15 regular employees;
2. Businesses eligible for reduction or exemption of acquisition tax or property tax pursuant to Article 75-2 (1) 2 and 4 of the Act: A project falling under any of the following items with total development project costs of at least 50 billion won;
(a) Where an enterprise city development district under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities (hereinafter in this Article referred to as an "enterprise city development district") is developed in accordance with an enterprise city development plan under Article 11 of that Act;
(b) Where a project implementer designated pursuant to Article 19 of the Regional Development and Support Act undertakes a regional development project to develop a regional development project district designated pursuant to Article 11 of that Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as a "regional development project district");
(c) Where a project implementer designated pursuant to Article 19 of the Regional Development and Support Act undertakes a regional development project to develop a regional revitalization area under Article 67 of that Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as a "regional revitalization area").
(2) In any of the following cases, the amount of acquisition tax or property tax reduced or exempted shall be collected pursuant to Article 75-2 (2) of the Act as specified in the relevant subparagraph: <Amended 2020.1.15>
1. In any of the following cases, the full amount of tax reduced or exempted during the 5 years preceding the date on which the relevant cause occurs shall be collected:
(a) Where the designation of an enterprise city development district is revoked pursuant to Article 7 of the Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities;
(b) Where an enterprise started in an enterprise city development district closes its business or closes a newly established place of business;
(c) Where the designation of a regional development project district is revoked pursuant to Article 18 of the Regional Development and Support Act or the designation of a regional revitalization area is revoked pursuant to Article 69 of that Act;
(d) Where an enterprise started in a regional development project district or regional revitalization area closes its business or closes a newly established place of business;
2. In any of the following cases, the full amount of tax reduced or exempted shall be collected:
(a) Where the criteria for reduction or exemption under paragraph (1) are not satisfied within 2 years from the end of the taxable year in which income first arises from the relevant business eligible for reduction or exemption (where no income arises from that business by the taxable year in which the third anniversary of the date of commencement of the business falls, meaning the taxable year in which that third anniversary falls; hereinafter the same shall apply in this item): Provided, That, with regard to the number of regular employees among the criteria in the items of paragraph (1) 1, collection shall not be made if the relevant criterion is satisfied in at least one of the taxable years ending within 2 years after the end of the taxable year in which income first arises from the relevant business eligible for reduction or exemption;
(b) Where, without justifiable grounds, the acquired real estate is not used directly for the relevant purpose by the time 3 years have elapsed from the date of acquisition, or is sold, donated, or used for another purpose before it has been used directly for the relevant purpose for 2 years.
(3) Article 11-2 (7) and (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees when applying paragraph (1) 1. <Added 2020.1.15, 2025.12.31, 2026.2.27>

Article 35-4 (Scope of Employment Crisis Areas)
"Areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 75-3 (1) 1 of the Act means areas designated and publicly notified by the Minister of Employment and Labor pursuant to Article 29 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on Employment Policy.

Article 35-5 (Reductions or Exemptions for Returned Granted Districts, etc.)
(1) "Types of business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the introductory part of Article 75-4 (1) of the Act means the types of business in Attached Table 2. In such cases, the types of business under subparagraphs 1 through 7, subparagraph 8 (a) through (g), and subparagraph 9 of Attached Table 2 shall be those under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification. <Amended 2025.12.31>
(2) "Place of business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the introductory part of Article 75-4 (1) of the Act means a place of business newly established (including relocation of an existing place of business) by a small and medium enterprise under the Framework Act on Small and Medium Enterprises to engage in a type of business under paragraph (1). In such cases, a place of business established by relocating an existing place of business shall be limited to a place of business relocated from the Seoul Metropolitan Area (excluding returned granted districts and areas surrounding returned granted districts under Article 2 of the Special Act on Support for Areas Surrounding Districts Granted to the United States Armed Forces in Korea, etc.). <Amended 2025.12.31>

Article 35-6 (Reductions or Exemptions for Areas with Declining Populations, etc.)
(1) "Types of business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 75-5 (1) of the Act means the types of business under Article 35-5 (1). <Amended 2025.12.31>
(2) "Place of business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 75-5 (1) of the Act means a place of business newly established (including relocation of an existing place of business) to engage in a type of business under paragraph (1). In such cases, a place of business established by relocating an existing place of business shall be limited to a place of business relocated from the Seoul Metropolitan Area (excluding areas with declining populations). <Amended 2025.12.31>
(3) "One house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 75-5 (4) of the Act means a case where a household composed of family members entered on the same household resident registration record as the acquirer as of the date of acquisition (excluding cohabitants) (the acquirer's spouse, the acquirer's unmarried lineal descendants under the age of 30, or, where the acquirer is unmarried and under the age of 30, his or her parents shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not entered on the same household resident registration record as the acquirer) owns 1 house in the Republic of Korea; a person who owns only land attached to a house, an association member's right of occupancy under subparagraph 2 of Article 13-3 of the Local Tax Act, or a right to acquire a house under a sales contract under subparagraph 3 of that Article shall also be deemed to own a house. <Added 2024.12.31, 2025.12.31>
(4) "House prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 75-5 (4) of the Act means a house satisfying all of the following requirements: <Amended 2025.12.31>
1. A house whose value at the time of acquisition under Article 10-3 or 10-4 of the Local Tax Act is not more than 300 million won (1.2 billion won in the case of a house located in an area with a declining population outside the Seoul Metropolitan Area);
2. A house located in an area falling under any of the following items:
(a) Areas with declining populations, excluding the Seoul Metropolitan Area (other than border areas under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Support for Border Areas), Metropolitan Cities (other than Gun areas), and a Special Self-Governing City;
(b) Areas of concern for population decline under subparagraph 12-2 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Local Decentralization and Balanced Regional Development, excluding the Seoul Metropolitan Area, Metropolitan Cities, and a Special Self-Governing City;
3. A house not located in an area subject to adjustment under Article 63-2 (1) 1 of the Housing Act;
4. In the case of a person who owns one house per household under paragraph (3), a house not located within the jurisdiction of the same Si/Gun/Gu as that one house per household.
(5) "Real estate prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 75-5 (7) of the Act means real estate falling under any of the following: <Added 2025.12.31>
1. Multi-unit housing with an exclusive floor area of not more than 85 square meters;
2. A multi-household house under subparagraph 1 (c) of Attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act for which the exclusive floor area of each unit is separately entered in the building register under Article 38 of the Building Act (limited to the portions corresponding to units with an exclusive floor area of not more than 85 square meters);
3. A general dormitory under subparagraph 2 (d) 1) of Attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
4. Land acquired to construct multi-unit housing, a multi-household house, or a general dormitory under subparagraphs 1 through 3.

Article 36 (Scope of Projects for Supply Purposes, etc.)
(1) "Projects prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 76 (1) and the main clause of paragraph (2) of that Article of the Act means, respectively, projects falling under any of the following: <Amended 2015.12.31, 2017.12.29, 2018.12.31, 2024.12.31>
1. Projects under Article 8 (1) 1 of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act (limited to cases where the State or a local government has directed or requested a purchase);
2. Projects under Article 8 (1) 2 (a) through (d) of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act;
3. Projects under Article 8 (1) 3 and 7 of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act: Provided, That projects for the construction, improvement, purchase, stockpiling, supply, lease, and management of neighborhood living facilities under subparagraph 14 (a) of Article 2 of the Housing Act or communal facilities under item (b) of that subparagraph shall be excluded;
4. Projects under Article 8 (1) 10 of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act (excluding projects entrusted by public institutions);
5. Projects for the construction and supply of public welfare facilities under the subparagraphs of Article 11 of the Enforcement Decree of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act pursuant to projects under subparagraphs 1 through 3 and projects under Article 8 (1) 4 and 5 of that Act;
6. Projects for stockpiling land for public development under Articles 14 and 15 of the Act on the Stockpiling of Public Land.
(2) The scope of public facilities, land attached thereto, and land for public facilities under Article 76 (2) of the Act shall be governed by Article 6. <Amended 2024.12.31>

Article 37 (Scope of Public Facilities, etc.)
The scope of public facilities, land attached thereto, and land for public facilities under Article 77 (2) of the Act shall be governed by Article 6.

Article 38 (Scope of Industrial Buildings, etc.)
"Industrial buildings, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory part of Article 78 (3) of the Act means buildings falling under any of the following: <Amended 2017.7.26, 2020.1.15, 2023.3.14, 2025.12.31>
1. Buildings for gas supply facilities under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Urban Gas Business Act (in the case of pipeline facilities under Article 5 (1) 4 of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act installed in industrial complexes under the Industrial Sites and Development Act, limited to pipeline facilities for supplying gas to the relevant areas);
2. Buildings for research and development facilities and pilot production facilities under the Act on Special Cases concerning Support for Industrial Technology Complexes;
3. Buildings for factories, knowledge industries, cultural industries, information and communications industries, and resource stockpiling facilities under Article 2 of the Industrial Sites and Development Act, and buildings for education, research, information processing, and distribution facilities directly related thereto: Provided, That buildings for factories shall satisfy the criteria for business types, floor area, etc. prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety;
4. Buildings installed by a managing agency under Article 30 (2) of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act for the management of an industrial complex, support for enterprises located therein, and employee welfare (excluding portions used for profit-making business);
5. Buildings for supply facilities under subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Integrated Energy Supply Act (in the case of pipeline facilities under Article 5 (1) 4 of the Enforcement Decree of the Local Tax Act installed in industrial technology complexes under the Act on Special Cases concerning Support for Industrial Technology Complexes, limited to pipeline facilities for supplying integrated energy to the relevant areas);
6. Industrial buildings falling under Article 6 (5) 1 through 5, 7, and 8 of the Enforcement Decree of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act.

Article 38-2 (Date of Commencement of Business of Foreign-Invested Enterprises, etc.)
① "Date of commencement of business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 78-3 (1) 1 of the Act means the date of commencement of business under Article 8 (1) of the Value-Added Tax Act.
② "Foreign investment ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 78-3 (1) 1 of the Act means the foreign investment ratio under Article 5 (3) of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act: Provided, That where a foreign investor under Article 2 (1) 5 of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act (hereinafter in this Article and Article 38-4 referred to as a "foreign investor") commenced foreign investment under subparagraph 4 of the same paragraph by December 31, 2002 in a domestic corporation newly established through capital contributions made, in accordance with a corporate reorganization plan, by creditor financial institutions of a domestic corporation whose corporate reorganization plan had been approved (hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as a "newly established corporation"), and completed payment of the objects of investment by that deadline, and preferred shares were issued as a result of the conversion of the liabilities of the newly established corporation into equity (limited to amounts converted into equity by December 31, 2002), the higher of the following ratios shall be the foreign investment ratio of the newly established corporation:
1. The foreign investment ratio calculated under Article 5 (3) of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act, including preferred shares;
2. The foreign investment ratio calculated under Article 5 (3) of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act, excluding preferred shares.
③ "Foreign investment made by a method prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the acquisition of a business" in the main clause of the introductory provisions of Article 78-3 (3) of the Act means the comprehensive or partial succession to rights and obligations relating to the business.
④ The amount corresponding to the ownership ratio of shares or equity interests (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "shares, etc.") or the amount corresponding to loans that is not treated as eligible for tax reduction or exemption under Article 78-3 (6) of the Act shall be the amount calculated according to the following classifications:
1. In cases falling under Article 78-3 (6) 1 of the Act: The amount calculated by multiplying the amount of foreign investment by a foreign corporation or foreign enterprise (hereinafter in this Article referred to as a "foreign corporation, etc.") by the ratio of shares, etc. of that foreign corporation, etc. directly or indirectly owned by nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc. under item (a) of that subparagraph (hereinafter in this Article and Article 38-4 referred to as "nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc.") (where the ratio is less than 5 percent, it shall be deemed to be 5 percent). In such cases, the ratio of direct or indirect ownership of shares, etc. shall be calculated as of the date on which the liability for the relevant local tax eligible for reduction or exemption under Article 78-3 (1) through (3) and (7) of the Act arises;
2. In cases falling under Article 78-3 (6) 2 of the Act: The portion of the foreign investment amount corresponding to the amount lent to a foreign investor by a person falling under any item of that subparagraph.
⑤ In applying paragraph ④ 1, the ratio of indirect ownership of shares, etc. shall be calculated according to the following classifications: Provided, That where there are two or more corporations that are shareholders of or contributors to a foreign corporation, etc. (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "shareholder corporations"), the sum of the ratios calculated for each shareholder corporation in accordance with the following subparagraphs shall be the ratio of indirect ownership of that foreign corporation, etc. by nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc.:
1. Where nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc. own at least 50 percent of the voting shares of a shareholder corporation of a foreign corporation, etc., the ratio of the voting shares of that foreign corporation, etc. owned by the shareholder corporation to the total number of voting shares issued by that foreign corporation, etc. (hereinafter in this Article referred to as the "share ownership ratio of the shareholder corporation");
2. Where nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc. own less than 50 percent of the voting shares of a shareholder corporation of a foreign corporation, etc., the ratio obtained by multiplying that ownership ratio by the share ownership ratio of the shareholder corporation.
⑥ The method of calculating the ratio of indirect ownership of shares, etc. under paragraph ⑤ shall also apply mutatis mutandis where one or more corporations are linked through share ownership relationships between a shareholder corporation of a foreign corporation, etc. and nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc.
⑦ "Country or region prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 78-3 (6) 3 of the Act means a country or region under Article 116-2 (13) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 38-3 (Method of Applying Reductions or Exemptions upon Capital Increases of Foreign-Invested Enterprises, etc.)
① Where local tax is reduced or exempted for an increase in the capital of a foreign-invested enterprise under Article 78-3 (7) of the Act, separate accounts shall be maintained for the business eligible for reduction or exemption related to the capital increase and for other businesses, and the foreign investment ratio under paragraph (1) 1 of that Article (hereinafter in this Article referred to as the "foreign investment ratio") shall be calculated on the basis of the business eligible for reduction or exemption for the capital increase. In such cases, Article 143 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the maintenance of separate accounts.
② Where local tax is reduced or exempted for an increase in the capital of a foreign-invested enterprise under Article 78-3 (7) of the Act, if the foreign-invested enterprise increases its capital within five years after a capital reduction for consideration (meaning a case in which its assets are actually reduced by the cancellation of shares or equity interests for consideration, the return of the amount of capital reduced, etc.) and applies for tax reduction or exemption, local tax shall be reduced or exempted only with respect to the foreign investment ratio corresponding to the portion that constitutes a net increase over the capital before the capital reduction for consideration.
③ "Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 78-3 (7) of the Act means making an additional investment for a business receiving local tax reduction or exemption under Article 78-3 (1) through (3) of the Act or Article 121-2 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
④ Where a foreign-invested enterprise that has received a decision granting local tax reduction or exemption for a capital increase under Article 78-3 (7) of the Act carries out a capital reduction for consideration within seven years after that capital increase, the amount of tax reduced or exempted shall be calculated by deeming that the capital has been reduced in reverse chronological order, beginning with the capital increase immediately preceding that capital reduction for consideration (excluding a capital increase in the form of shares issued through the capitalization of reserves and revaluation reserves under Article 5 (2) 2 of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act and reserves under other statutes or regulations).
⑤ "Grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions of Article 78-3 (9) of the Act other than the formula means a case satisfying all of the following requirements:
1. Before increasing its capital, the foreign-invested enterprise must have received local tax reduction or exemption under Article 78-3 (1) through (3) of the Act or Article 121-2 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act for a business under any subparagraph of Article 121-2 (1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as the "business eligible for reduction or exemption before the capital increase"), the period of that reduction or exemption must have expired, and the enterprise must have received, through a capital increase under Article 78-3 (7) of the Act, a decision granting reduction or exemption for a business under any subparagraph of Article 121-2 (1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as the "business eligible for reduction or exemption for the capital increase");
2. Business fixed assets of the business eligible for reduction or exemption before the capital increase, for which the reduction or exemption period under Article 78-3 (1) through (3) of the Act or Article 121-2 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act has expired, must continue to be used in the business eligible for reduction or exemption for the capital increase, and, as of the date on which the registration of a change concerning the capital increase is made, the value of the business fixed assets of that business eligible for reduction or exemption before the capital increase must account for at least 30 percent of the total value of the business fixed assets of the business eligible for reduction or exemption for the capital increase.

Article 38-4 (Additional Collection of Tax Reduced or Exempted for Foreign-Invested Enterprises, etc.)
① The additional collection of acquisition tax and property tax under Article 78-3 (12) of the Act shall be governed by the following classifications: <Amended on 2021.2.17>
1. In cases under Article 78-3 (12) 1 and 2 of the Act: Acquisition tax and property tax shall each be additionally collected in an amount calculated by multiplying the amount of that tax reduced or exempted within the five years preceding the date of transfer of shares, etc. or the date on which the ratio of shares, etc. falls below the required ratio by the ratio transferred or the shortfall ratio;
2. In cases under Article 78-3 (12) 3 and 4 of the Act: Acquisition tax and property tax reduced or exempted within the five years preceding the date of cancellation of registration or the date of business closure (meaning the earlier of the date of business closure and the date of cancellation under Article 8 (8) and (9) of the Value-Added Tax Act) shall each be additionally collected;
3. In cases under Article 78-3 (12) 5 of the Act: Acquisition tax and property tax reduced or exempted within the five years (three years in cases of failure to meet the employment-related criteria for tax reduction or exemption) preceding the date on which five years (three years in cases of failure to meet the employment-related criteria for tax reduction or exemption) have elapsed after the filing of the foreign investment report shall each be additionally collected;
4. In cases under Article 78-3 (12) 6 and 7 of the Act: The amounts of acquisition tax and property tax reduced or exempted within the five years preceding the date on which the relevant ground for additional collection arises shall each be additionally collected. In such cases, the tax additionally collected shall be limited to the portion for which the relevant ground for additional collection has arisen.
② Where grounds under the subparagraphs of Article 78-3 (12) of the Act arise simultaneously, the ground resulting in the greater amount of tax to be additionally collected under the subparagraphs of paragraph ① shall apply; where grounds under the subparagraphs of Article 78-3 (12) of the Act arise successively, they shall be applied successively in the order in which they arise, beginning with the earliest ground, up to the amount of tax reduced or exempted.
③ In cases falling under Article 78-3 (13) 1 and 3 through 5 of the Act, the acquisition tax and property tax reduced or exempted shall not be additionally collected.
④ "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 78-3 (13) 5 of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on 2025.12.30>
1. Where a ground for additional collection of acquisition tax and property tax under Article 78-3 (12) of the Act arises after a development project implementer under Article 8-3 (1) and (2) of the Special Act on Designation and Management of Free Economic Zones has completed a development project for a free economic zone under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of that Act;
2. Where a ground for additional collection of acquisition tax and property tax under Article 78-3 (12) of the Act arises after an enterprise city development project implementer designated under Article 10 (1) of the Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities has completed a development project for an enterprise city development zone under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of that Act;
3. Where a ground for additional collection of acquisition tax and property tax under Article 78-3 (12) of the Act arises after a project implementer designated under Article 8 (1) of the Special Act on Promotion and Support for the Saemangeum Project has completed a development project for the Saemangeum project area under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of that Act;
4. Where a ground for additional collection of acquisition tax and property tax under Article 78-3 (12) of the Act arises after a development project implementer for a Jeju investment promotion zone designated under Article 162 of the Special Act on the Establishment of Jeju Special Self-Governing Province and the Development of Free International City has completed a development project for the Jeju investment promotion zone;
5. Where a foreign investor that invested in a business involving technologies of new growth engine industries under Article 121-2 (1) 1 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act transfers the business eligible for reduction or exemption or the shares, etc. it owns to nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc., and the Minister of Finance and Economy confirms that there is no impediment to the enterprise independently producing, in the Republic of Korea, the products or services produced or provided in the business involving those technologies of new growth engine industries;
6. Where a foreign investor transfers the shares, etc. it owns to nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc. pursuant to other statutes or regulations or government policies, and the Minister of Finance and Economy confirms this;
7. Where, after a foreign investor transfers the shares, etc. it owns to nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc., the transferees who are nationals of the Republic of Korea, etc. transfer those shares, etc. to another foreign investor within seven days, and the Minister of Finance and Economy confirms that there is no impediment to continuing to carry out the original business.
⑤ The procedures for confirmation under paragraph ④ 5 through 7 shall be governed by Article 116-10 (3) through (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
⑥ In applying Article 78-3 (14) of the Act, where a ground falling under any of subparagraphs 3 through 7 of paragraph (12) of that Article arises, the acquisition tax and property tax reductions or exemptions under paragraphs (1) through (3) and (7) of that Article shall not apply to the remaining reduction or exemption period after the date on which that ground arises (including the relevant taxable year if the ground arises before the property tax assessment reference date). The same shall also apply where, during the remaining reduction or exemption period after the date on which a ground falling under any of subparagraphs 3 through 7 of Article 78-3 (12) of the Act arises, the criteria for tax reduction or exemption under paragraph (1) of that Article and the introductory provisions of Article 121-2 (1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act are met again.

Article 39 (Scope of Large Cities) "Large cities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 79 (1) of the Act means overcrowding control areas (excluding industrial complexes subject to the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act).

Article 39-2 (Scope of Enterprises Starting Businesses in Opportunity Development Special Zones) "Enterprises starting businesses in business categories prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory provisions of Article 80-2 (1) of the Act means enterprises that do not fall under any of the subparagraphs of Article 58-3 (6) of the Act and start businesses in the business categories specified in attached Table 3. In such cases, the business categories under subparagraphs 1 through 8 of attached Table 3 and subparagraph 9 (a) through (g) of that Table shall be business categories under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification. <Amended on 2025.12.31>

Article 40 (Scope of One House per Household) "One house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory provisions of Article 81 (3) of the Act means the first acquisition of one house by a single household consisting of family members (excluding cohabitants) who are listed in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer as of the date of acquisition (the acquirer's spouse and the acquirer's unmarried lineal descendants under 30 years of age shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not listed in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer), in an area classified in the following subparagraphs, after the date of public notice of the relocation plan for the relevant institution under Article 16 (5) of the Special Act on the Construction of the Multifunctional Administrative City in the Yeongi-Gongju Area for Follow-up Measures for the New Administrative Capital, the date of approval of the regional relocation plan under Article 4 (4) of the Special Act on the Creation and Development of Innovation Cities, or the date of commencement of operations (applicable only to cases under Article 81 (3) 1 (c) of the Act). In such cases, ownership solely of land appurtenant to a house shall also be deemed ownership of a house. <Amended on 2013.1.1, 2016.12.30, 2018.2.27>
1. For persons eligible for reduction or exemption under Article 81 (3) 1 (a) of the Act: The following areas:
(a) Where a relocating public institution under Article 81 (1) of the Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as a "relocating public institution") relocates to a joint innovation city under Article 31 of the Special Act on the Creation and Development of Innovation Cities: Within the Metropolitan City, Province, or Special Self-Governing Province that jointly constructed the innovation city;
(b) In cases other than those under item (a): Areas according to the following classifications:
      1) Until June 30, 2012: Within the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Province, or Special Self-Governing Province in which the relocating public institution is located, or the planned area under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Special Act on the Construction of the Multifunctional Administrative City in the Yeongi-Gongju Area for Follow-up Measures for the New Administrative Capital (hereinafter in this Article referred to as the "planned area");
      2) On or after July 1, 2012: Within the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Province, or Special Self-Governing Province in which the relocating public institution is located;
2. For persons eligible for reduction or exemption under Article 81 (3) 1 (b) and (c) of the Act: Areas according to the following classifications:
(a) Until June 30, 2012: Within the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Province, or Special Self-Governing Province in which the central administrative agency, etc. under Article 81 (3) of the Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as a "central administrative agency, etc.") is located, or within the planned area;
(b) On or after July 1, 2012: Within the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, or Special Self-Governing Province in which the central administrative agency, etc. is located.

Article 40-2 (Scope of One House per Household for Korean Employees of United States Forces Korea) "Cases resulting in one house per household prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory provisions of Article 81-2 (1) of the Act means cases in which a single household consisting of family members (excluding cohabitants) who are listed in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer as of the date of acquisition (the acquirer's spouse and the acquirer's unmarried lineal descendants under 30 years of age shall each be deemed to belong to the same household even if they are not listed in the same household resident registration record as the acquirer) owns one house in Pyeongtaek City; ownership solely of land appurtenant to a house shall also be deemed ownership of a house.

Article 41 (Persons Eligible for Reduction or Exemption, Including Merchants Operating Shops) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 83 (3) of the Act means merchants who, as of the date of authorization to implement a market redevelopment project, have continuously operated shops in the existing traditional market (meaning a traditional market under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Special Act on the Development of Traditional Markets and Shopping Districts; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) for at least the preceding three years, or persons who own real estate in the traditional market as of the date of authorization to implement the market redevelopment project. <Amended on 2024.12.31>

Article 41-2 (Local Government Investment Ratios in Local Public Enterprises, etc. and Scope of Public Facilities)
① "Local government investment ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 85-2 (1) 1 of the Act means the ratio according to the following classifications:
1. Investment ratio in a local public corporation established under Article 49 of the Local Public Enterprises Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as a "local public corporation"): The ratio of the amount invested by a local government (where two or more local governments jointly established the corporation, the sum of the amounts invested by each local government) to the capital of the local public corporation: Provided, That where a local public corporation has issued shares under Article 53 (3) of the Local Public Enterprises Act, it means the ratio of the number of shares owned by a local government (including shares deemed to have been invested by a local government under paragraph (4) of that Article) (where two or more local governments own shares, the sum of the numbers of shares owned by each local government) to the total number of those issued shares;
2. Investment ratio in an institution invested in or funded by a local government that has been designated and publicly notified under Article 5 of the Act on the Operation of Institutions Invested in or Funded by Local Governments (hereinafter in this Article referred to as a "local government-invested or -funded institution"): The ratio of the amounts invested or contributed by a local government (including amounts deemed to have been invested or contributed by a local government under Article 4 (2) of that Act and, where two or more local governments have invested or contributed, the sum of the amounts invested or contributed by each local government) to the capital or contributed funds of the local government-invested or -funded institution.
② The scope of public facilities and land appurtenant thereto, and sites for public facilities, under Article 85-2 (1) 4 of the Act shall be governed by Article 6. <Amended on 2024.12.31>

Section 8 Support for Public Administration, etc.

Article 42 (Scope of Businesses Eligible for Exemption for Political Parties, etc.)
① "Land appurtenant to a building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 89 (2) of the Act means land appurtenant to a building under construction for direct use in the relevant business, or land appurtenant to a planned building for which construction could not commence due to construction restriction measures taken by an administrative agency after the building permit was granted.
② "A license for a political party to use directly for its business" in the main clause of Article 89 (3) of the Act means a license necessary for a political party under Article 89 (1) of the Act to operate its nonprofit business, or a license where all proceeds generated from the business facilities or activities under that license are used for the nonprofit business.
③ "The business establishment portion and employee portion of resident tax relating to profit-making businesses, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 89 (3) of the Act means the business establishment portion of resident tax (limited to the amount of tax imposed under Article 81 (1) 2 of the Local Tax Act) and the employee portion of resident tax imposed on the basis of business establishments and employees directly employed in profit-making businesses. In such cases, where a building is used jointly for a business eligible for exemption and a profit-making business, or employees perform duties for both, the principal use or duties shall govern. <Amended on 2014.3.14, 2020.12.31>

Article 43 (Definition of Village Associations, etc.) "Residents' communities, such as village associations, prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the introductory provisions of Article 90 (1) of the Act means organizations consisting solely of village residents for the purpose of promoting the welfare of village residents, etc. <Amended on 2011.12.31>

Article 44 Deleted <2015.12.31>

Chapter III Special Provisions on Local Income Tax <Newly inserted on 2014.3.14>

Section 1 Tax Credits and Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Global Income <Newly inserted on 2014.3.14>

Article 45 (Tax Credit for Bookkeeping)
① "Unavoidable grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as a natural disaster" in the proviso to Article 93 (2) 2 of the Act means cases falling under any subparagraph of Article 116-3 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② A person who intends to receive a tax credit for bookkeeping under Article 93 of the Act shall apply to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment by attaching an application for a tax credit for bookkeeping prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the final return of the tax base: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax credit to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 116-3 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for a tax credit against individual local income tax under Article 93 of the Act. <Amended on 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

Article 46 (Method of Calculating Dividend Income Eligible for Dividend Tax Credit) In applying Article 95 of the Act, the calculation of the amount of dividend income exceeding the threshold amount for global taxation of interest income, etc. specified in paragraph (3) of that Article shall be governed by Article 116-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.

Article 46-2

Article 47 (Tax Credit for Disaster Losses)
① "Assets prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of the introductory provisions of Article 96 (1) of the Act means assets falling under any subparagraph of Article 118 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② In applying Article 96 (1) of the Act, the calculation of the ratio of damage caused by a disaster shall be governed by Article 118 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
③ A person who intends to receive a tax credit for disaster losses under Article 96 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax credit for disaster losses prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment within the deadline according to the following classifications: <Amended on 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. For individual local income tax for which the deadline for filing the final return of the tax base has not passed: That filing deadline: Provided, That where the period from the date of the disaster to the filing deadline is less than one month, the deadline shall be the date on which one month has elapsed after the date of the disaster;
2. For individual local income tax unpaid as of the date of the disaster and individual local income tax payable, other than that under subparagraph 1: One month from the date of the disaster.
④ The calculation of the ratio of assets lost under Article 96 (7) of the Act shall be governed by Article 118 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.

Article 48 (Foreign Tax Credit for Global Income, etc.)
① "Amount of foreign income tax prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 97 (1) of the Act means the amount of tax under Article 117 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② A person who intends to receive a foreign tax credit under Article 97 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a foreign tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment or to the person responsible for special collection when filing the final return of the tax base or making the year-end tax settlement for the taxable period in which the foreign-source income is included: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax credit to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 117 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for a tax credit against individual local income tax under Article 97 of the Act. <Amended on 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

Article 48-2 (Tax Credit for Pension Accounts)
① A person who intends to receive a tax credit for pension accounts under Article 97-3 (1) of the Act shall submit the certificate of pension payments under Article 118-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act to the person responsible for special collection, the taxpayers' association, or the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment by the date under each subparagraph of Article 113 (1) of that Enforcement Decree: Provided, That where the certificate of pension payments has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 118-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, it shall be deemed to have also been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.
② In applying paragraph ①, where documentary evidence for a tax credit has been submitted to the Commissioner of the National Tax Service under Article 216-3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, the documents under Article 118-2 (2) of that Enforcement Decree may be submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment by the date under each subparagraph of Article 113 (1) of that Enforcement Decree: Provided, That where they have been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 118-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, they shall be deemed to have also been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.
③ Where a pension account holder has an amount of pension premiums paid into a pension account in a previous taxable period for which the tax credit for pension accounts under Article 97-3 of the Act was not received, and applies to the pension account operator to convert all or part of that amount into pension premiums paid into the pension account in the relevant taxable period, in applying Article 97-3 of the Act, the amount for which conversion is requested shall be deemed to have been withdrawn first from the pension account and then paid again into that pension account as pension premiums on the date of the application. In such cases, the amount for which conversion is requested shall be deemed pension premiums paid into the pension account on the date of the application and shall satisfy the requirements in each subparagraph of Article 40-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
④ Matters necessary for applications to convert pension premiums paid under paragraph ③, etc. shall be governed by Article 118-3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.

Article 48-3 (Tax Credit for Insurance Premiums)
① "Premiums for protection-type insurance exclusively for persons with disabilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (1) 1 of the Act means insurance premiums and mutual aid contributions under Article 118-4 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② "Insurance premiums prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (1) 2 of the Act means insurance premiums and mutual aid contributions under Article 118-4 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.

Article 48-4 (Tax Credit for Medical Expenses)
① "Medical expenses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory provisions of Article 97-4 (2) of the Act means medical expenses falling under any subparagraph of Article 118-5 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② The medical expenses under paragraph ① shall not include expenses under Article 118-5 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
③ When making the year-end settlement of tax on wage and salary income under Article 103-15 of the Local Tax Act, a person responsible for special collection shall, for an employee with medical expenses eligible for a special tax credit, submit a tape or diskette containing computerized statements of that employee's medical expense payments to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment when submitting the statements of wage and salary income payments under Article 215 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act: Provided, That where a tape or diskette containing computerized statements of the relevant employee's medical expense payments has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 118-5 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, it shall be deemed to have also been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.

Article 48-5 (Tax Credit for Educational Expenses)
① "Educational expenses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the introductory provisions of Article 97-4 (3) of the Act means educational expenses falling under any subparagraph of Article 118-6 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② "Educational courses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (3) 1 (b) of the Act means educational courses under Article 118-6 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
③ "Overseas educational institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (3) 1 (c) of the Act means educational institutions under Article 118-6 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
④ "Students prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (3) 1 (c) of the Act means students under Article 118-6 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
⑤ "Sports facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (3) 1 (d) of the Act means sports facilities falling under any subparagraph of Article 118-6 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
⑥ "Amounts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (3) 1 (d) of the Act means tuition fees under Article 118-6 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
⑦ "Cases of receiving subsidies, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 97-4 (3) 2 (c) of the Act means cases of receiving support under Article 118-6 (11) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act. <Amended on 2026.2.27>
⑧ "Special education expenses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the introductory provisions of Article 97-4 (3) 3 of the Act means expenses under Article 118-6 (14) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act. <Amended on 2026.2.27>
⑨ "Social welfare facilities and nonprofit corporations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (3) 3 (a) of the Act means the facilities and corporations under the subparagraphs of Article 118-6 (15) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act. <Amended on 2026.2.27>
⑩ "Institutions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (3) 3 (b) of the Act means institutions under Article 118-6 (16) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act. <Amended on 2026.2.27>

Article 48-6 (Tax Credit for Donations, etc.)
① When making the year-end settlement of tax on wage and salary income or tax on business income under Article 103-15 of the Local Tax Act, a person responsible for special collection shall, for a resident to whom the tax credit for donations applies, submit a tape or diskette containing computerized statements of that resident's donations to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment when submitting the payment statements under Article 164 of the Income Tax Act: Provided, That where a tape or diskette containing computerized statements of the relevant employee's donations has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 118-7 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, it shall be deemed to have also been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.
② "Calculated amount of individual local income tax on global income attributable to wage and salary income prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 97-4 (7) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the calculated tax on global income for the relevant taxable period by the ratio of the amount of wage and salary income to the amount of global income for that taxable period.
③ Where, after a person who received a tax credit for donations under paragraph ① dies, a person entitled to a legally reserved portion of inheritance claims the return of trust property under Article 1115 of the Civil Act and receives its return, the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the address of the person entitled to the legally reserved portion shall additionally collect from that person the amount calculated by multiplying the amount under subparagraph 1 by the ratio under subparagraph 2:
1. The amount of individual local income tax corresponding to the amount for which the resident received the tax credit for donations in taxable periods falling within the exclusion period for assessment under Article 38 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes as of the date on which the person entitled to the legally reserved portion receives its return;
2. The ratio obtained by dividing the amount returned to the person entitled to the legally reserved portion by the value of the trust property at the time that person receives the return of the legally reserved portion.

Article 48-7 (Scope of Compliant Business Operators) "Business operators satisfying requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as reporting a business account" in the main clause of Article 97-4 (9) of the Act means business operators satisfying all requirements in the subparagraphs of Article 118-8 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.

Article 49 (Tax Reduction or Exemption for Wage and Salary Income)
① Where a business eligible for reduction or exemption under Article 98 (1) of the Act or another Act is operated concurrently with other businesses, the common necessary expenses and common revenue of the business eligible for reduction or exemption and the other businesses shall be calculated separately in accordance with Article 119 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② A person who intends to receive a reduction of or exemption from tax on wage and salary income under Article 98 (1) 1 of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, through the person paying the wage and salary income in the Republic of Korea, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over special collection by the tenth day of the month following the month for which the reduction or exemption is sought: Provided, That where the person applies for income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 138 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for a tax reduction or exemption for individual local income tax under Article 98 (1) of the Act. <Amended on 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

Article 50 (Tax Reduction or Exemption for Income from International Transportation)
① "Income from the international transportation business of ships and aircraft, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 98 (1) 2 of the Act means income falling under any subparagraph of Article 119-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
② A person who intends to receive a reduction of or exemption from tax on income derived from an international transportation business under Article 98 (1) 2 of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment together with a return under Article 93 (5) or 95 of the Local Tax Act: Provided, That where the person applies for income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 138 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for a tax reduction or exemption for individual local income tax under Article 98 (1) of the Act. <Amended on 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

SECTION 2 SPECIAL CASES FOR SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES <Newly Inserted on March 14, 2014>

Article 51 (Scope of Small and Medium Enterprises)
The scope of small and medium enterprises under the portion of Article 99 (1) of the Act other than its subparagraphs shall be governed by Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 52 (Leases Excluded from Investment Tax Credits)
"Leases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the portion of Article 99 (1) of the Act other than its subparagraphs, Article 103 (1) of the Act, the portion of Article 109 (1) of the Act other than its subparagraphs, the former part of the portion of Article 110 (1) of the Act other than its subparagraphs, Article 111 (1) of the Act, the former part of Article 112 (1) of the Act, the former part of Article 113 (1) of the Act, and the main clause of the portion of Article 114 (1) of the Act other than its subparagraphs each mean leases under Article 3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 53 (Investment Tax Credits for Small and Medium Enterprises)
(1) Where a small and medium enterprise acquires business assets, point-of-sale information management system equipment, or information protection system equipment used jointly for a business falling within the scope of small and medium enterprises under Article 2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act and another business, Article 99 of the Act shall apply by deeming such assets to be assets of the business that primarily uses them.

(2) "Business assets prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 99 (1) 1 of the Act means assets under Article 4 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) Matters necessary for calculation of the amount invested under Article 99 (3) of the Act shall be governed by Article 4 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) A person seeking an investment tax credit under Article 99 of the Act shall submit an application for an investment tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the investment completion date falls (meaning each taxable year in which the investment is made, where the person seeks application of paragraph (2) of that Article): Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax credit pursuant to Article 4 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax credit under Article 99 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; February 3, 2015; July 26, 2017>

Article 54 (Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Newly Established Small and Medium Enterprises)
(1) "Enterprises prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the portion of Article 100 (2) of the Act other than its subparagraphs means enterprises under Article 5 (4) and (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on December 30, 2016>

(2) Deleted. <December 30, 2016>

(3) Deleted. <December 30, 2016>

(4) Deleted. <December 30, 2016>

(5) "Small and medium enterprises engaged in new energy technologies prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 100 (4) of the Act means small and medium enterprises manufacturing products specified in the subparagraphs of Article 5 (10) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(6) Calculation of income arising from the relevant business under Article 100 (5) of the Act shall be governed by Article 5 (11) and (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(7) "Business assets prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as land, buildings, and machinery" in the proviso of Article 100 (6) 1 of the Act means land and depreciable assets under Article 24 of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act.

(8) "Ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 100 (6) 1 of the Act means 30 percent.

(9) In applying Article 100 (6) of the Act, classification of businesses of the same kind shall follow the detailed classifications under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification.

(10) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 100 (1), (2), (4), or (7) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Articles 5 (16) and 99-6 (11) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 100 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 55 (Special Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Small and Medium Enterprises)
(1) "Contract manufacturing business under an original equipment manufacturing arrangement prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 101 (1) 1 (v) of the Act means a business under Article 6 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Motor vehicle repair shop prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 101 (1) 1 (z) of the Act means a motor vehicle repair shop under Article 54 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) "Small enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 101 (1) 2 (a) of the Act means an enterprise under Article 6 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) "Knowledge-based industry prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 101 (1) 2 (e) of the Act means a business falling under any subparagraph of Article 6 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 101 of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 6 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 101 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

SECTION 3 SPECIAL CASES FOR RESEARCH AND HUMAN RESOURCES DEVELOPMENT <Newly Inserted on March 14, 2014>

Article 56 (Tax Credits for Research and Human Resources Development Expenses)
(1) "Research and development expenses in new growth engine industries prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the portion of Article 102 (1) 1 of the Act other than its items means expenses under Article 9 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on December 30, 2016>

(2) Deleted. <December 30, 2016>

(3) "Where an enterprise ceases to qualify as a small and medium enterprise for the first time, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 102 (1) 3 (b) 2) of the Act means a case under Article 9 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "middle-standing enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in 3) of the same item means an enterprise meeting all the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 9 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) Calculation of the annual average amount of general research and human resources development expenses incurred over four years under Article 102 (2) of the Act shall be governed by Article 9 (5) through (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) A domestic person seeking application of Article 102 (1) 1 of the Act shall account separately for new growth engine research and development expenses, original technology research and development expenses, and general research and human resources development expenses, each in separate accounts. In such cases, where new growth engine research and development expenses or original technology research and development expenses are also attributable to general research and human resources development, the entire amount of those expenses shall be treated as general research and human resources development expenses. <Amended on December 30, 2016>

(6) A domestic person seeking application of Article 102 (1) of the Act shall, when filing the tax base return, submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment an application for a tax credit, a statement of research and human resources development expenses, a research and development plan, and other supporting documents, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety: Provided, That, where the domestic person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax credit pursuant to Article 9 (9) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the domestic person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax credit under Article 102 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 57 (Scope of Facilities for Research and Testing)
(1) "Middle-standing enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 103 (1) of the Act means an enterprise meeting all the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 10 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Newly Inserted on August 20, 2014>

(2) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 103 (2) 1 of the Act means facilities under Article 10 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 2 of the same paragraph means facilities under Article 10 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014>

(3) Deleted. <December 30, 2016>

(4) Calculation of the amount invested under Article 103 (3) and (4) of the Act shall be governed by Article 4 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014>

(5) A person seeking an investment tax credit under Article 103 of the Act shall submit an application for a tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the investment completion date falls (meaning each taxable year in which the investment is made, where the person seeks application of paragraph (3) of that Article; hereinafter the same shall apply in Articles 62 (2), 63 (2), 64 (2), 65 (2), and 66 (2)): Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax credit pursuant to Article 10 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax credit under Article 103 of the Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 58 (Scope of Technical Know-How)
(1) "Specially related person prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104 (1) and (2) of the Act means a specially related person under Article 98 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.

(2) "Technical know-how prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104 (1) of the Act means technical know-how under Article 11 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "technology prescribed by Presidential Decree" means technology under Article 11 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(3) A person seeking application of Article 104 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption or an application for a tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction, exemption, or credit pursuant to Article 11 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction, exemption, or credit under Article 104 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; February 3, 2015; July 26, 2017>

Article 59 (Reduction of or Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax for High-Technology Enterprises Located in Special Research and Development Zones)
(1) "Businesses prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the biotechnology industry and the information and communications industry" in Article 105 (1) of the Act means businesses engaging in the industries specified in the subparagraphs of Article 11-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Cumulative amount invested prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 105 (3) 1 of the Act means the aggregate amount invested under Article 11-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The amount of individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 105 (5) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (where the amount is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases for two consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year in which the reduction or exemption was granted, the amount for the second taxable year shall be the amount remaining after subtracting the amount paid for the first taxable year). That amount shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreases.

Total tax reduced or exempted under Article 105 (3) 2 of the Act in taxable years falling within the two years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the enterprise's number of regular employees decreases − (Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreases × 1 million won)

(4) The scope of regular employees and the method of calculating the number of regular employees under Article 105 (6) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(5) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 105 (7) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 11-2 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 105 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; February 27, 2026>

Article 60 (Scope of Foreign Engineers)
(1) "Foreign engineer prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 106 (1) of the Act means a person who does not hold the nationality of the Republic of Korea and falls under any subparagraph of Article 16 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Advanced technology prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 106 (2) of the Act means technology under Article 16 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 106 (1) or (2) of the Act shall, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, submit an application for tax reduction or exemption through the special collection agent to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over special collection by the 10th day of the month following the month in which the person provided services: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over withholding for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 16 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 106 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

