(1) "Young persons, persons aged 60 or older, and persons with disabilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 116 (1) of the Act means persons in the respective categories specified in the subparagraphs of Article 27 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) In applying paragraph (1), persons falling under any subparagraph of Article 27 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall be excluded.

(3) "Enterprises prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 116 (1) of the Act means enterprises under Article 27 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) An employee seeking application of Article 116 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by documents proving the period of military service, etc., to the special collection agent by the last day of the month following the month in which the date of employment falls: Provided, That, where the employee has applied to the withholding agent for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 27 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the employee shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 116 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; February 3, 2015; July 26, 2017>

(5) The special collection agent shall also submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over special collection the materials submitted to the tax office head having jurisdiction over withholding pursuant to Article 27 (6) and (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(6) Where a person has earned income received from a small and medium enterprise under Article 116 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to in this Article as "income eligible for reduction or exemption") and other global income, the tax reduction or exemption for the relevant taxable period shall be 10 percent of the tax reduction or exemption under Article 27 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(7) In granting an earned income tax credit under Article 94 of the Act, where a person has income eligible for reduction or exemption and other earned income (including where the person has no earned income other than income eligible for reduction or exemption), the amount calculated using the following formula shall be the earned income tax credit:

Amount of tax credit = Earned income tax credit calculated pursuant to Article 94 of the Act × (1 − Proportion of the employee's total gross salary represented by the total gross salary received from a small and medium enterprise under Article 116 (1) of the Act)

