(2) A person seeking a tax credit pursuant to Article 117 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax credit pursuant to Article 30-2 (3) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax credit under Article 117 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

