(6) A small and medium enterprise seeking application of Article 118 (1) of the Act shall, when filing the tax base return for the relevant taxable year, submit an application for a tax credit and a statement of calculation of the tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment: Provided, That, where the enterprise applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax credit pursuant to Article 30-4 (3) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, it shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax credit under Article 118 (1) of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

