Article 74 (Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Business Conversion by Enterprises Receiving Support to Respond to Trade Changes)
(1) Fixed assets for business under the main clause of Article 121 (1) of the Act shall be assets under Article 30 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Business conversion eligible for application of Article 121 (1) of the Act shall be business conversion under Article 30 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The tax reduced or exempted pursuant to Article 121 (1) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula:

Individual local income tax on capital gains calculated pursuant to Articles 103 and 103-2 of the Local Tax Act on the transfer of the business premises building and its appurtenant land of the business before conversion × Ratio of the acquisition cost of machinery for the converted business to the transfer value of the business before conversion

(4) In applying paragraph (3), where the fixed assets for the converted business, or the machinery, business premises building, and its appurtenant land for the converted business, have not been acquired by the end of the business year in which the date of transfer of the fixed assets for the business before conversion falls, their acquisition costs shall be the planned values in the statement of (planned) business conversion.

(5) The tax payable pursuant to the former part of Article 121 (2) of the Act shall be the amounts specified in the following subparagraphs:

1. Where individual local income tax on capital gains has been reduced or exempted pursuant to paragraph (3): The entire tax reduced or exempted;

2. Where a tax reduction or exemption has been granted based on the planned values under paragraph (4): The amount of reduction or exemption received in excess of the amount calculated pursuant to paragraph (3) based on actual values.

(6) "Additional amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 121 (2) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the reduced or exempted tax payable pursuant to paragraph (5) by the period in subparagraph 1 and the rate in subparagraph 2:

1. The period from the day following the end of the taxable year in which the reduction or exemption was received to the end of the taxable year in which the grounds for payment arise;

2. Three ten-thousandths per day.

(7) In applying Article 121 of the Act, businesses shall be classified according to the most detailed classifications under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification.

(8) A resident seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 121 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption and a statement of (planned) business conversion prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the fixed assets for the business before conversion falls: Provided, That, where the resident applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 30 (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the resident shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 121 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(9) Where the converted business commences after application of paragraph (4), a report on completion of business conversion prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety shall be submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the business commencement date falls: Provided, That, where a report on completion of business conversion has been submitted to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 30 (13) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, it shall be deemed to have also been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

