(1) "Business conversion date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the portion of Article 122 (1) of the Act other than its subparagraphs means a date falling under any subparagraph of Article 30-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Business conversion under Article 122 (1) 2 of the Act shall be business conversion under Article 30-2 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) "Taxable year prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 122 (2) of the Act means a taxable year under Article 30-2 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) In applying Article 122 of the Act, businesses shall be classified according to the most detailed classifications under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification.

(5) "Additional amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 122 (4) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the amount equivalent to the tax payable pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article by the period in subparagraph 1 and the rate in subparagraph 2:

1. The period from the day following the end of the taxable year in which the reduction or exemption was received to the end of the taxable year in which a ground specified in Article 122 (3) of the Act arises;

2. Three ten-thousandths per day.

(6) A domestic person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 122 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the business conversion date falls: Provided, That, where the domestic person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 30-2 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the domestic person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 122 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 76 (Special Cases of Individual Local Income Taxation for Transfers of Assets by Shareholders, etc.)
(1) "Amount equivalent to the amount of a gift prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 123 (1) of the Act means the amount calculated pursuant to Article 37 (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Of the tax reduced or exempted for shareholders, etc. pursuant to Article 123 (1) of the Act, the amount collected by adding it to the corporate local income tax payable by the relevant corporation pursuant to paragraph (2) of that Article shall be 10 percent of the amount calculated under each item of Article 37 (15) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Newly Inserted on August 20, 2014>

(3) "Additional amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 123 (3) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the tax under paragraph (2) by the period in subparagraph 1 and the rate in subparagraph 2: <Newly Inserted on August 20, 2014>

1. The period from the day following the end of the business year in which the tax under paragraph (2) was not paid to the end of the business year in which that tax is paid;

2. Three ten-thousandths per day.

(4) Shareholders, etc. seeking application of Article 123 (1) of the Act shall submit an asset sale and purchase agreement, a gift agreement, and a statement of (planned) debt repayment and an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the assets pursuant to that paragraph falls: Provided, That, where the shareholders, etc. apply to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 37 (25) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, they shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 123 of the Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

SECTION 8 SPECIAL CASES FOR BALANCED DEVELOPMENT AMONG REGIONS <Newly Inserted on March 14, 2014>

Article 77 (Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Small and Medium Enterprises Relocating outside the Overconcentration Control Zone in the Seoul Metropolitan Area)
(1) Cases eligible for tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 124 (1) of the Act shall be cases under Article 60 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "area prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 124 (1) of the Act means an area under Article 60 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Tax calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the portion of Article 124 (2) of the Act other than its subparagraphs means individual local income tax reduced or exempted pursuant to Article 124 (1) of the Act after the factory relocation date. In such cases, where two or more factories have relocated outside the overconcentration control zone in the Seoul Metropolitan Area and Article 124 (2) 3 of the Act applies (excluding establishment of the head office), the amount shall be limited to the tax reduced or exempted for relocation of a factory producing the same products as those of the factory established within the overconcentration control zone in the Seoul Metropolitan Area.

(3) "Where a factory is relocated outside the overconcentration control zone in the Seoul Metropolitan Area and business commences, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 124 (2) 2 of the Act means a case in which a factory is relocated and business commences as prescribed in paragraph (1).

(4) A person seeking application of Article 124 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption and a statement of calculation of the tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 60 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 124 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(5) "Classification prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 124 (5) of the Act means a detailed classification under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification.

Article 78 (Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Enterprises Located in Agro-Industrial Complexes)
(1) "Agro-industrial complex prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 125 (1) 1 of the Act means an agro-industrial complex under Article 61 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "district or area prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 2 of the same paragraph means an area under Article 61 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) A person seeking application of Article 125 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for an income tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 61 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 125 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 79 (Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax for Members of Farming Association Corporations)
(1) Dividend income exempted pursuant to the former part of Article 126 (1) of the Act shall be dividend income exempt from income tax pursuant to Article 63 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Calculation of dividend income under the latter part of Article 126 (1) of the Act shall be governed by Article 63 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) "Farmer prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 126 (2) of the Act means a farmer under Article 66 (4) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act and Article 63 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) "Farmer prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 126 (5) of the Act, the former part of Article 128 (1) of the Act, and paragraph (2) of that Article means a farmer under Article 66 (7) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the former part of Article 68 (2) of that Act, paragraph (3) of that Article, and Article 63 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) Farmland for which income arising from a contribution in kind pursuant to Article 126 (2) or 128 (1) of the Act is exempt from individual local income tax on capital gains shall be farmland under Article 63 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(6) Article 63 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to payment of tax under Article 126 (3) of the Act, and the amount of tax shall be 10 percent of the amount calculated under that paragraph.

(7) A person seeking exemption from individual local income tax on dividend income pursuant to Article 126 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the farming association corporation when receiving the relevant dividend income, and the farming association corporation shall submit the application for tax exemption filed by the member to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over special collection by the last day of the month following the month in which the dividend payment date falls: Provided, That, where an application for income tax exemption is made to the tax office head having jurisdiction over withholding pursuant to Article 63 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for individual local income tax exemption under Article 126 (1) of the Act shall be deemed to have also been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(8) "Amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 126 (4) and (8) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the amount equivalent to the tax payable pursuant to Article 126 (3) and (7) of the Act by the period in subparagraph 1 and the rate in subparagraph 2:

1. The period from the day following the deadline for payment upon preliminary filing of individual local income tax on capital gains for the farmland, etc. originally contributed in kind to the date of payment under Article 126 (3) or (7) of the Act;

2. Three ten-thousandths per day.

(9) A person seeking exemption from, or carryover taxation of, individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 126 (2) or (5) of the Act shall submit an application for tax exemption or an application for carryover taxation prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by a copy of the contribution in kind agreement, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return; an application for carryover taxation shall be submitted jointly with the farming association corporation: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for exemption from, or carryover taxation of, capital gains tax pursuant to Article 63 (10) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for exemption from, or carryover taxation of, individual local income tax under Article 126 (2) or (5) of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(10) In applying Article 126 (7) of the Act, the criteria for determining whether at least 50 percent of the shares or equity interests acquired through a contribution in kind have been disposed of shall be governed by Article 28 (10) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(11) Payment of tax under Article 126 (7) of the Act shall be made where the aggregate of the period of direct use of the relevant real estate before the contribution in kind and the period from the contribution in kind to the date of disposal of the shares or equity interests is less than eight years. In such cases, in calculating the period of use of inherited real estate, the period during which the decedent used the real estate shall be deemed a period during which the heir used it.

(12) Except as prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (11), Article 63 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to exemption under Article 126 of the Act.

Article 80 (Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax for Members of Fisheries Association Corporations)
(1) "Amount within the scope prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 127 (1) of the Act means the amount under Article 64 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Fisher prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 127 (2) of the Act means a person under Article 64 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) "Land, etc. for fisheries prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 127 (2) of the Act means land and buildings under Article 64 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) The tax payable pursuant to Article 127 (3) of the Act shall be 10 percent of the amount calculated pursuant to Article 64 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 127 (3) of the Act means cases in which all household members leave the country for emigration under the Emigration Act.

(6) A person seeking exemption from individual local income tax on dividend income pursuant to Article 127 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the fisheries association corporation when receiving the relevant dividend income, and the fisheries association corporation shall submit the application for tax exemption filed by the member to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over special collection by the last day of the month following the month in which the dividend payment date falls: Provided, That, where an application for income tax exemption is made to the tax office head having jurisdiction over withholding pursuant to Article 64 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for individual local income tax exemption under Article 127 (1) of the Act shall be deemed to have also been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(7) A person intending to apply for exemption from individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 127 (1) and (2) of the Act shall submit an application for tax exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by one copy of the contribution in kind agreement, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the relevant land, etc. for fisheries falls: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for capital gains tax exemption pursuant to Article 64 (9) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for individual local income tax exemption under Article 127 (1) and (2) of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 81 (Reduction of or Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax for Farmers)
(1) Dividend income arising from agricultural income under Article 128 (3) of the Act means the amount calculated pursuant to Article 65 (2) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) A person seeking carryover taxation of individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 128 (2) of the Act shall submit an application for carryover taxation prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return, and the application for carryover taxation shall be submitted jointly with the agricultural company: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for carryover taxation of capital gains tax pursuant to Article 65 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for carryover taxation of individual local income tax under Article 128 (1) of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; January 15, 2020>

(3) A person seeking exemption from individual local income tax on dividend income pursuant to Article 128 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for tax exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the farming association corporation when receiving the relevant dividend income, and the farming association corporation shall submit the application for tax exemption filed by the member to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over special collection by the last day of the month following the month in which the dividend payment date falls: Provided, That, where an application for income tax exemption is made to the tax office head having jurisdiction over withholding pursuant to Article 65 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for individual local income tax exemption under Article 128 (3) of the Act shall be deemed to have also been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 82 (Reduction of or Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Self-Cultivated Farmland)
(1) "Residents residing where the farmland is located who are prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 129 (1) of the Act means persons under Article 66 (1) and (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Direct payment subsidies for transfer of farm management prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 129 (1) of the Act means farmland transfer retirement subsidies under Article 4 of the Regulations on Implementation of the Direct Payment System for Producers of Agricultural Products, and "corporations prescribed by Presidential Decree" means corporations under Article 66 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on March 26, 2024>

(3) "Direct cultivation by a method prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 129 (1) of the Act means cultivation or growing under Article 66 (13) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "land prescribed by Presidential Decree" means farmland under Article 66 (4), (5), (11), and (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) "Income prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 129 (1) of the Act means the amount calculated pursuant to Article 66 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) "Where a ground prescribed by Presidential Decree arises" in Article 129 (2) of the Act means a case falling under any subparagraph of Article 66 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(6) A person intending to apply for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 129 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the relevant farmland falls; where the farmland has been transferred to a corporation under paragraph (2), the application for tax reduction or exemption shall be submitted jointly with the transferee: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for a capital gains tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 66 (9) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 129 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(7) Upon receiving an application for tax reduction or exemption under paragraph (6), the head of the relevant local government shall immediately notify the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment of the corporation under paragraph (2) thereof.

Article 83 (Reduction of or Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Land for Livestock Sheds)
(1) "Resident prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 130 (1) of the Act means a person under Article 66-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; "direct livestock farming by a method prescribed by Presidential Decree" means that under Article 66-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; and "land for livestock sheds prescribed by Presidential Decree" means land for livestock sheds under Article 66-2 (3) through (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Closure of business under the main clause of Article 130 (1) of the Act shall mean a case in which closure has been confirmed in a certificate of the period of livestock farming and closure of business pursuant to Article 66-2 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The tax reduced or exempted pursuant to Article 130 (1) of the Act shall be calculated using the following formula:

Tax reduced or exempted = Calculated individual local income tax on capital gains × [Area of land for livestock sheds (where it exceeds 990 square meters, it shall be 990 square meters) ÷ Total area transferred]

(4) "Income prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 130 (1) of the Act means the amount calculated pursuant to Article 66-2 (10) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as inheritance" in the proviso of Article 130 (2) of the Act means cases under Article 66-2 (11) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(6) A person intending to apply for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 130 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety and the certificate of the period of livestock farming and closure of business under paragraph (2) to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable period in which the date of transfer of the relevant land for livestock sheds falls: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for a capital gains tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 66-2 (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 130 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 84 (Requirements for Reduction of or Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Replacement of Farmland)
(1) "Resident prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 131 (1) of the Act means a person under Article 67 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; "direct cultivation by a method prescribed by Presidential Decree" means cultivation or growing under Article 67 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; and "cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" means cases falling under Article 67 (3) through (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014>

(2) "Income prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 131 (1) of the Act means the amount calculated pursuant to Article 67 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) "Land prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 131 (2) of the Act means farmland falling under any subparagraph of Article 67 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) A person intending to apply for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 131 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the relevant farmland falls: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for a capital gains tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 67 (9) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for an individual local income tax reduction or exemption under Article 131 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(5) "Ground prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 131 (4) of the Act means a case falling under any subparagraph of Article 67 (10) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(6) "Amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 131 (5) of the Act shall be the amount calculated by multiplying the amount equivalent to the tax payable pursuant to Article 131 (4) of the Act by the period in subparagraph 1 and the rate in subparagraph 2:

1. The period from the day following the deadline for payment upon preliminary filing of individual local tax on capital gains for the former farmland to the date of payment of individual local tax on capital gains under Article 131 (4) of the Act;

2. Three ten-thousandths per day.

Article 84-2 (Special Cases of Taxation of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains from Sale and Purchase of Farmland for Business Recovery Support)
(1) A person seeking a refund pursuant to Article 131-2 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for refund prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 67-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment: Provided, That, where the person applies to the tax office head having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment for a refund of capital gains tax pursuant to Article 67-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed to have also applied for a refund of individual local income tax on capital gains under Article 131-2 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(2) Article 60 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes shall apply mutatis mutandis where the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment makes a refund upon receiving an application for refund pursuant to paragraph (1). In such cases, the provisions concerning additional amounts on local tax refunds under Article 62 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes shall not apply. <Amended on March 27, 2017>

(3) Where a farmer who has received a refund of individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 131-2 (1) of the Act again transfers repurchased farmland, etc., Article 82 shall apply by deeming the period during which the farmer cultivated the farmland, etc. within the lease period under Article 24-3 (3) of the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act to be a period of direct cultivation of the farmland, etc. by that farmer.

(4) Where repurchase of part of the farmland, etc. has been requested pursuant to Article 19-6 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Korea Rural Community Corporation and Farmland Management Fund Act, the tax refunded under paragraph (2) shall be the amount equivalent to the individual local income tax on capital gains paid for the repurchased farmland, etc.

SECTION 9 SPECIAL CASES FOR SUPPORTING PUBLIC WORKS PROJECTS <Newly inserted on March 14, 2014>

Article 85 (Reduction or Exemption of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains from Land, etc. for Public Works Projects)
(1) "Bonds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 132 (1) of the Act other than its subparagraphs means compensation bonds under Article 72 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; "Acts prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the Special Act on the Construction of Bogeumjari Housing, Etc." means any of the Acts specified in the subparagraphs of Article 72 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; and "method prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the method under Article 72 (3) of that Decree.
(2) Where a person who has transferred land, etc. for a public works project intends to receive a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 132 (2) of the Act, the implementer of a public works project under Article 132 (1) 1 of the Act or a project implementer under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph (hereinafter referred to as a "project implementer" in this Article) shall, within two months from the date on which the implementer is designated as such, submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by documents verifying that the implementer is the relevant project implementer, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the transferor's place of tax payment: Provided, That where an application for income tax reduction or exemption is made to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the transferor's place of tax payment pursuant to Article 72 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 132 (2) of the Act shall also be deemed to have been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(3) "Deadline prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 132 (3) 2 of the Act means the deadline under Article 72 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
(4) Where any person has entered into a special agreement to hold compensation bonds until maturity pursuant to Article 132 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "party to a special agreement" in this Article), the project implementer shall notify the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment of the details of compensation for that party by the end of the following month, and, where a party to a special agreement breaches that agreement, shall notify that head of the breach by the end of the following month: Provided, That where the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment has been notified of the breach pursuant to Article 72 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment shall also be deemed to have been notified.
(5) A project implementer intending to apply for a reduction or exemption under Article 132 (6) of the Act shall, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the relevant land, etc. falls, submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the transferor's place of tax payment an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by documents verifying that the implementer is the relevant project implementer (including, in the case of a party to a special agreement, documents verifying the conclusion of the special agreement and the deposit of the compensation bonds): Provided, That where the project implementer applies for income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the transferor's place of tax payment pursuant to Article 72 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 132 (6) of the Act shall also be deemed to have been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(6) A person intending to apply for a reduction or exemption under Article 132 (7) of the Act shall, together with the tax base return (including a preliminary return) for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the relevant land, etc. falls, submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by documents verifying the expropriation (including, in the case of a party to a special agreement, documents verifying the conclusion of the special agreement and the deposit of the compensation bonds): Provided, That where an application for capital gains tax reduction or exemption is made to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 72 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 132 (7) of the Act shall also be deemed to have been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 86 (Reduction or Exemption of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains from Land, etc. Subject to Purchase Due to Designation of Development Restriction Zones)
(1) "Resident prescribed by Presidential Decree who resides in the area where the relevant land, etc. is located" in Article 133 (1) 1 and 2 and (2) 1 and 2 of the Act respectively means a person who has resided in an area falling under any subparagraph of Article 74 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (including an area that fell within such an area when the person began residing there but ceased to do so due to reorganization of administrative districts, etc.).
(2) "Area prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as designation as a free economic zone under the Special Act on Designation and Management of Free Economic Zones" in the proviso to the part of Article 133 (2) of the Act other than its subparagraphs means an area falling under any subparagraph of Article 74 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
(3) A person intending to apply for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax on capital gains pursuant to Article 133 (4) of the Act shall, together with the tax base return (including a preliminary return) for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the relevant land, etc. falls, submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by documents verifying that a request to purchase the land was made or that the land was purchased through consultation: Provided, That where an application for capital gains tax reduction or exemption is made to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 74 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 133 of the Act shall also be deemed to have been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(4) The period of residence under Article 133 (4) of the Act shall be calculated in accordance with Article 74 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 87 (Tax Reduction or Exemption for Relocation to Local Areas of Factories in Planned Development Districts of the Multifunctional Administrative City or Innovation Cities)
(1) "Outside the multifunctional administrative city, etc., as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 134 (1) of the Act means an area under Article 79-3 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and a factory under Article 134 (1) of the Act shall be a factory under Article 54 (1) of that Decree.
(2) Relocation to a local area to which Article 134 (1) of the Act applies shall be relocation to a local area under Article 79-3 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.
(3) A person intending to apply for a reduction or exemption under Article 134 (2) of the Act shall, upon acquiring a factory in a local area and commencing business, submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the business commencement date falls: Provided, That where an application for income tax reduction or exemption is made to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 85-2 (5) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 134 of the Act shall also be deemed to have been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 88 (Reduction or Exemption of Individual Local Income Tax, etc. for Social Enterprises and Standard Workplaces for Persons with Disabilities)
(1) "Amount calculated as an additional amount equivalent to interest prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 135 (5) of the Act means an amount calculated by applying Article 75 (4) mutatis mutandis.
(2) A person intending to apply for a reduction or exemption under Article 135 (6) of the Act shall submit an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where an application for income tax reduction or exemption is made to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 79-7 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 135 of the Act shall also be deemed to have been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 89 (Application for Reduction or Exemption of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains from Mountainous Districts Transferred to the State)
A person intending to apply for a reduction or exemption under Article 136 (2) of the Act shall, when filing the tax base return (including a preliminary return) for the taxable year in which the date of transfer of the relevant mountainous district falls, submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment an application for tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by a copy of the sales contract verifying that the Minister of the Korea Forest Service purchased it pursuant to Article 18 (2) of the State Forest Administration and Management Act: Provided, That where an application for capital gains tax reduction or exemption is made to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 79-11 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, an application for reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 136 of the Act shall also be deemed to have been made. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

SECTION 10 SPECIAL CASES FOR STABILIZING PEOPLE'S LIVELIHOODS <Newly inserted on March 14, 2014>

Article 90 (Tax Credits for Investments in Facilities to Promote Workers' Welfare)
(1) "Domestic person prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 137 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means a person who newly constructs or purchases a facility falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 94 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; "unsold housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in that part means housing under Article 94 (2) of that Decree; "facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 137 (1) 4 of the Act means facilities under Article 94 (3) of that Decree; and "facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 137 (1) 5 of the Act means facilities under Article 94 (4) of that Decree.

(2) The amount of a tax credit under Article 137 (2) of the Act shall be an amount equivalent to 10 percent of the tax credit calculated under Article 94 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) A person seeking application of Article 137 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the relevant facility was acquired: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax credit to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 94 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a tax credit for individual local income tax under Article 137 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(4) Where unsold housing under paragraph (1) is acquired, Article 97 (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the submission of relevant supporting documents, and the preparation and retention of relevant supporting documents shall be governed by Article 98-4 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) "Additional amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 137 (4) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the amount of the tax credit received by the period specified in subparagraph 1 and the rate specified in subparagraph 2:

1. The period from the day following the date of filing the tax base return for the taxable year for which the tax credit was received to the date of filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which a ground under Article 137 (4) of the Act arose;

2. Three ten-thousandths per day.

Article 91 (Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Lessors of Small Housing)
(1) "Domestic person prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 138 (1) of the Act means a domestic person who satisfies all the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 96 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Rental housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 138 (1) of the Act means private rental housing under Article 2 of the Special Act on Private Rental Housing and public rental housing under subparagraph 1 (a) of Article 2 of the Special Act on Public Housing that a domestic person under paragraph (1) has registered as rental housing and that satisfies all the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 96 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on December 28, 2015>

(3) The criteria for determining whether at least three units of rental housing have been leased for at least five years under Article 138 (1) and (2) of the Act shall be as specified in the subparagraphs of Article 96 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) "Where unavoidable grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree exist" in the proviso to Article 138 (3) of the Act means any case falling under the subparagraphs of Article 96 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(5) A person seeking application of Article 138 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 96 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the relevant taxable year: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 96 (6) of that Decree, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 138 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; February 3, 2015; July 26, 2017>

Article 92 (Reduction of or Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains from Long-Term Rental Housing)
(1) "Resident prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part of Article 139 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means a resident who leases at least five units of rental housing.

(2) Where a building used for another purpose, such as commercial premises, is situated in part of rental housing constructed for lease under the proviso to Article 139 (1) of the Act or on the same lot, the scope of the property treated as housing and the calculation of necessary expenses shall be governed by Article 122 (4) and (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.

(3) A person intending to apply for a tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 139 (3) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 97 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for the taxable year in which the relevant rental housing was transferred: Provided, That where the person applies for a capital gains tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 97 (4) of that Decree, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 139 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(4) The calculation of the lease period for rental housing under Article 139 (4) of the Act shall be governed by Article 97 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) The head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment who receives an application for a tax reduction or exemption pursuant to Article 139 (3) of the Act shall verify a certified copy of the register or certified copies of the land register and building register for the rental housing through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act.

Article 93 (Exemption from Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains from Newly Constructed Rental Housing)
(1) "Resident prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 140 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means a resident under Article 97-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Article 92 (2) through (5) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the reporting of housing lease particulars, applications for tax reductions or exemptions, calculation of lease periods, etc. for newly constructed rental housing under Article 140 (1) of the Act; in the case of rental housing acquired for lease under Article 140 (1) 2 of the Act, a copy of the sale and purchase agreement and supporting documents proving the date of payment of the contract deposit shall be attached in addition to the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 92 (3) and submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment: Provided, That where a person applies for special cases concerning a capital gains tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 97-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for exemption from individual local income tax under Article 140 of the Act.

Article 94 (Special Taxation for Unsold National Housing)
(1) "Unsold national housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 141 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means housing no larger than the national housing size that satisfies all the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 98 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act and is located outside the Seoul Special Metropolitan City.

(2) Where a resident owns a house other than unsold national housing under paragraph (1) acquired between November 1, 1995 and December 31, 1997 (including cases in which a sale and purchase agreement was concluded and the contract deposit paid by December 31, 1997) and transfers that other house, the provisions on one house for one household under Article 89 (1) 3 of the Income Tax Act shall apply by taking into account only houses other than the relevant unsold national housing.

(3) The calculation of the holding period for unsold national housing under Article 141 (1) of the Act shall be governed by Article 95 (4) of the Income Tax Act.

(4) A person intending to apply for special taxation pursuant to Article 141 (1) of the Act shall submit a report on the application of special taxation for unsold national housing prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by the following documents, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the final tax base return for the taxable year in which the relevant house was transferred (including a preliminary return where the method under subparagraph 1 of the same paragraph has been selected): Provided, That where the person applies for special taxation of capital gains tax to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 98 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for special taxation of individual local income tax under Article 141 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; December 30, 2016; July 26, 2017>

1. A copy of the certificate of unsold national housing issued by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu;

2. A copy of the sale and purchase agreement made upon acquisition of the unsold national housing (limited to cases in which acquisition is registered on or after January 1, 1998).

(5) "Unsold national housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 141 (3) of the Act means housing no larger than the national housing size that satisfies all the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 98 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act and is located outside the Seoul Special Metropolitan City.

(6) Where a resident owns a house other than unsold national housing under paragraph (5) acquired between March 1, 1998 and December 31, 1998 (including cases in which a sale and purchase agreement was concluded and the contract deposit paid by December 31, 1998) and transfers that other house, the provisions on one house for one household under Article 89 (1) 3 of the Income Tax Act shall apply by taking into account only houses other than the relevant unsold national housing.

(7) Paragraph (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to applications for special taxation under Article 141 (3) of the Act, and the calculation of the holding period for unsold national housing shall be governed by Article 95 (4) of the Income Tax Act.

Article 95 (Special Taxation of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains, etc. for Acquisition of Unsold Housing in Regions)
(1) "Unsold housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 142 (1) of the Act means housing falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 98-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "unsold housing").

(2) A person seeking special taxation pursuant to Article 142 of the Act shall submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the final or preliminary tax base return for the taxable year in which the relevant house is transferred, a copy of the sale and purchase agreement bearing a seal affixed by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu to certify that the house is unsold housing pursuant to Article 98-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, or the following documents: Provided, That where a copy of the sale and purchase agreement, etc. has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment together with a capital gains tax base return pursuant to Article 98-2 (2) of that Decree, it shall be deemed also to have been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Amended on December 30, 2016>

1. Housing under Article 98-2 (1) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act: A certificate of unsold housing confirmed by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu and a copy of the sale and purchase agreement;

2. Housing under Article 98-2 (1) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act: Documents confirming the fact of project plan approval or the fact of application for project plan approval, as verified by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu, and a copy of the sale and purchase agreement.

(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), Article 98-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of special taxation under Article 142 of the Act.

Article 96 (Special Taxation of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Acquirers of Unsold Housing)
(1) "Unsold housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 143 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means housing under Article 98-3 (1) and (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) A person seeking special taxation pursuant to Article 143 of the Act shall submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the preliminary or final tax base return for individual local income tax on capital gains from the relevant house, a copy of the sale and purchase agreement bearing a seal affixed by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu to certify that the house is unsold housing pursuant to Article 98-3 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act; for housing under the part of Article 143 (2) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs, the person shall submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment a copy of the construction commencement report submitted to the head of a Si/Gun/Gu and documents verifying that an inspection for use or approval for use (including temporary approval for use) has been obtained: Provided, That where a copy of the sale and purchase agreement, etc. has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment together with a capital gains tax base return pursuant to Article 98-3 (5) of that Decree, it shall be deemed also to have been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Amended on December 30, 2016>

(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), Article 98-3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of special taxation under Article 143 of the Act.

Article 97 (Special Taxation of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Acquirers of Unsold Housing Located Outside the Seoul Metropolitan Area)
(1) "Unsold housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 145 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means housing under Article 98-4 (1) and (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) The rate of reduction in the sale price under Article 145 (1) of the Act shall be the rate calculated under Article 98-4 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) A person seeking special taxation pursuant to Article 145 of the Act shall submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the preliminary or final tax base return for individual local income tax on capital gains from the relevant unsold house, a copy of the sale and purchase agreement bearing a seal affixed by the head of a Si/Gun/Gu to certify that the house is unsold housing pursuant to Article 98-4 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act: Provided, That where a copy of the sale and purchase agreement, etc. has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment together with a capital gains tax base return pursuant to Article 98-4 (5) of that Decree, it shall be deemed also to have been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Amended on December 30, 2016>

(4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), Article 98-4 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of special taxation under Article 145 of the Act.

Article 98 (Special Taxation of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Acquirers of Housing Remaining Unsold after Completion)
(1) "Business operator prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 146 (1) 1 of the Act means a person falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 98-5 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "housing remaining unsold after completion prescribed by Presidential Decree" means housing under Article 98-5 (2) and (3) of that Decree.

(2) In applying Article 146 (1) of the Act, the lease period for the relevant housing remaining unsold after completion means the period calculated under Article 98-5 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) A person seeking special taxation pursuant to Article 146 of the Act shall submit the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 98-5 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the preliminary or final tax base return for individual local income tax on capital gains from the relevant housing remaining unsold after completion: Provided, That where a copy of the sale and purchase agreement, etc. has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment together with a capital gains tax base return pursuant to Article 98-5 (6) of that Decree, it shall be deemed also to have been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.

(4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), Article 98-5 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of special taxation under Article 146 of the Act.

Article 99 (Special Taxation of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Acquirers of Unsold Housing)
(1) "Unsold housing prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 147 (1) of the Act means housing under Article 98-6 (1) and (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "business operator prescribed by Presidential Decree" means a person falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 98-6 (3) of that Decree.

(2) A person seeking special taxation pursuant to Article 147 of the Act shall submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment a copy of the sale and purchase agreement issued by a project owner, etc. pursuant to Article 98-6 (8) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, together with the preliminary or final tax base return for individual local income tax on capital gains from the relevant unsold house: Provided, That where a copy of the sale and purchase agreement, etc. has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment together with a capital gains tax base return pursuant to Article 98-6 (5) of that Decree, it shall be deemed also to have been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.

(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), Article 98-6 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of special taxation under Article 147 of the Act.

Article 100 (Special Taxation of Individual Local Income Tax on Capital Gains for Acquirers of Newly Constructed Housing, etc.)
(1) "Newly constructed housing, unsold housing, or housing owned by a person in a household owning only one house, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 148 (1) of the Act means housing classified as follows:

1. New housing or unsold housing: Housing under Article 99-2 (1) and (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;

2. Housing owned by a person in a household owning only one house: Housing under Article 99-2 (3) through (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Person prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 148 (1) of the Act means a person in the applicable category specified in the subparagraphs of Article 99-2 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) A person seeking special taxation pursuant to Article 148 of the Act shall submit to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the preliminary or final tax base return for capital gains from the relevant house, a copy of the sale and purchase agreement issued with a seal certifying that the house is newly constructed housing, unsold housing, or housing owned by a person in a household owning only one house pursuant to Article 99-2 (11) or (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act: Provided, That where a copy of the sale and purchase agreement, etc. has been submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment together with a capital gains tax base return pursuant to Article 99-2 (8) of that Decree, it shall be deemed also to have been submitted to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.

(4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), Article 99-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of special taxation under Article 148 of the Act.

SECTION 11 OTHER SPECIAL CASES CONCERNING LOCAL INCOME TAX <Newly inserted on March 14, 2014>

Article 101 (Applications for Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Income from Forest Development)
A domestic person seeking application of Article 149 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 102 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 149 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 102 (Applications for Tax Credits for Third-Party Logistics Expenses)
A person seeking an individual local income tax credit pursuant to Article 150 (1) and (2) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax credit to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 104-14 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a tax credit for individual local income tax under Article 150 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 103 (Tax Credits for Expenses for Customized University Education, etc.)
(1) "Facilities for research and human resource development prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 151 (2) of the Act means facilities under Article 104-17 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Advance employment contracts, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 151 (4) of the Act means contracts falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 104-17 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) "Expenses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 151 (4) of the Act means expenses under Article 104-17 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 104 (Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Enterprises Returning to Korea after Expanding Overseas)
(1) "Nationals of the Republic of Korea and other persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 152 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means nationals of the Republic of Korea under Article 104-21 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Where a place of business is relocated or returned to Korea pursuant to Article 152 (1) of the Act, the type of business conducted at the place of business before the relocation or return and the type of business conducted at the place of business after the relocation or return shall be the same at the class level of the Korean Standard Industrial Classification.

(3) "Where the person fails to relocate or return a place of business to Korea and commence business as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 152 (4) 2 of the Act means a case in which the requirements specified in the subparagraphs of Article 104-21 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act are not met.

(4) The tax amount payable pursuant to Article 152 (4) of the Act shall be the full amount of individual local income tax reduced or exempted pursuant to Article 152 (2) and (3) of the Act.

(5) A person seeking application of Article 152 (1) through (3) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption and a statement of calculation of the tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 104-21 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 152 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 105 (Criteria, etc. for Reductions of or Exemptions from Individual Local Income Tax for Foreign Investment)
(1) The criteria for foreign investment under Article 153 (1) of the Act shall be as prescribed in Article 116-2 (1) through (10) and (16) through (21) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Foreign investment ratio calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 153 (2) of the Act means the foreign investment ratio under Article 116-2 (14) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) In applying Article 153 (7) of the Act, the amount corresponding to the ownership ratio of shares, etc. or the amount corresponding to loans that is not considered eligible for a tax reduction or exemption shall be the amount calculated under Article 116-2 (11) and (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) "Foreign investment made in a manner prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the acquisition of a business" in Article 153 (8) of the Act means foreign investment under Article 116-2 (15) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) "Cumulative amount of foreign investment prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 153 (10) 1 (a) of the Act means the cumulative amount of foreign investment under Article 116-2 (22) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(6) The amount of individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 153 (12) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (if the result is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases in two consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year for which a reduction or exemption was received, the amount for the second taxable year means the amount after subtracting the amount paid in the first taxable year), and shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased:

[Sum of tax amounts reduced or exempted under Article 153 (10) 2 of the Act for taxable years within the two years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the relevant enterprise's number of regular employees decreased] - [(Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for a reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased) × 1,000,000 won]

(7) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees under Article 153 (13) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(8) "Tax amount calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 153 (14) of the Act means the tax amount under Article 116-7 (1), (4), and (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, and "additional amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the amount calculated under Article 116-7 (3) of that Decree.

Article 106 (Reductions of or Exemptions from Individual Local Income Tax for Enterprises Located in the Jeju Advanced Science and Technology Complex)
(1) "Businesses prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the biotechnology industry and the information and communications industry" in Article 154 (1) of the Act means businesses engaged in the industries specified in the subparagraphs of Article 116-14 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Cumulative investment amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 154 (2) 1 of the Act means the total investment amount under Article 116-14 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The amount of individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 154 (4) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (if the result is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases in two consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year for which a reduction or exemption was received, the amount for the second taxable year means the amount after subtracting the amount paid in the first taxable year), and shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased:

[Sum of tax amounts reduced or exempted under Article 154 (2) 2 of the Act for taxable years within the two years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the relevant enterprise's number of regular employees decreased] - [(Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for a reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased) × 1,000,000 won]

(4) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees under Article 154 (5) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(5) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 154 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 116-14 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 154 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 107 (Reductions of or Exemptions from Individual Local Income Tax for Enterprises Located in Jeju Investment Promotion Zones or Jeju Free Trade Zones)
(1) "Investment meeting the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 155 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means investment classified as follows:

1. Businesses under Article 155 (1) 1 of the Act: Investment under Article 116-15 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;

2. Businesses under Article 155 (1) 2 of the Act: Investment under Article 116-15 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;

3. Businesses under Article 155 (1) 3 of the Act: Investment under Article 116-15 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Cumulative investment amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 155 (3) 1 of the Act means the total investment amount under Article 116-15 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The amount of individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 155 (5) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (if the result is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases in two consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year for which a reduction or exemption was received, the amount for the second taxable year means the amount after subtracting the amount paid in the first taxable year), and shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased:

[Sum of tax amounts reduced or exempted under Article 155 (3) 2 of the Act for taxable years within the two years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the relevant enterprise's number of regular employees decreased] - [(Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for a reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased) × 1,000,000 won]

(4) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees under Article 155 (6) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(5) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 155 (2) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 116-15 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 155 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

(6) The additional collection of individual local income tax amounts reduced or exempted for enterprises located in Jeju Investment Promotion Zones or Jeju Free Trade Zones under Article 155 (8) of the Act shall be governed by the criteria specified in the subparagraphs of Article 116-17 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 108 (Reductions of or Exemptions from Individual Local Income Tax for Newly Established Enterprises, etc. in Enterprise City Development Zones, etc.)
(1) "Investment meeting the criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 156 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means investment classified as follows:

1. Businesses under Article 156 (1) 1, 3, and 5 of the Act: Investment under Article 116-21 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;

2. Businesses under Article 156 (1) 2, 4, and 6 of the Act: Investment under Article 116-21 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Income eligible for a reduction or exemption from a business operated at a place of business in the relevant zone by an enterprise that is newly established or establishes a new place of business in an enterprise city development zone, a development promotion district in a new development region, an investment promotion district in a new development region, or an exposition site development project area falling under Article 156 (1) 1, 3, and 5 of the Act shall be income directly generated from facilities in which investment was made in the relevant zone to operate a business eligible for a reduction or exemption under paragraph (1) 1.

(3) "Cumulative investment amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 156 (3) 1 of the Act means the total investment amount under Article 116-21 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) The individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 156 (5) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (if the result is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases in two consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year for which a reduction or exemption was received, the amount for the second taxable year means the amount after subtracting the amount paid in the first taxable year), and shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased:

[Sum of tax amounts reduced or exempted under Article 156 (3) 2 of the Act for taxable years within the two years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the relevant enterprise's number of regular employees decreased] - [(Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for a reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased) × 1,000,000 won]

(5) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees under Article 156 (6) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(6) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 156 (2) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 116-21 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 156 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 109 (Reductions of or Exemptions from Individual Local Income Tax for Enterprises, etc. Located in Investment Promotion Zones in the Hub City of Asian Culture)
(1) Investments for which individual local income tax is reduced or exempted pursuant to Article 157 (1) of the Act shall be investments under Article 116-25 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Cumulative investment amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 157 (3) 1 of the Act means the total investment amount under Article 116-25 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The amount of individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 157 (5) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (if the result is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases in two consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year for which a reduction or exemption was received, the amount for the second taxable year means the amount after subtracting the amount paid in the first taxable year), and shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased:

[Sum of tax amounts reduced or exempted under Article 157 (3) 2 of the Act for taxable years within the two years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the relevant enterprise's number of regular employees decreased] - [(Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for a reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased) × 1,000,000 won]

(4) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees under Article 157 (6) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(5) The amount of individual local income tax additionally collected pursuant to Article 157 (7) of the Act shall be the full amount of tax reduced or exempted.

(6) A person intending to apply for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 157 (9) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 116-25 (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 157 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 110 (Reductions of or Exemptions from Individual Local Income Tax for Newly Established Enterprises, etc. in Financial Hubs)
(1) "Criteria prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 158 (1) of the Act means the criteria under Article 116-26 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) Income generated from a business eligible for a reduction or exemption at a place of business within a financial hub under Article 158 (2) of the Act shall be income under Article 116-26 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) "Cumulative investment amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 158 (3) 1 of the Act means the total investment amount under Article 116-26 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) The amount of individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 158 (5) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (if the result is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases in two consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year for which a reduction or exemption was received, the amount for the second taxable year means the amount after subtracting the amount paid in the first taxable year), and shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased:

[Sum of tax amounts reduced or exempted under Article 158 (3) 2 of the Act for taxable years within the two years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the relevant enterprise's number of regular employees decreased] - [(Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for a reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased) × 1,000,000 won]

(5) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees under Article 158 (6) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(6) The amount of individual local income tax additionally collected pursuant to Article 158 (7) of the Act shall be the full amount of tax reduced or exempted.

(7) A person intending to apply for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 158 (9) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 116-26 (9) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 158 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 111 (Reductions of or Exemptions from Individual Local Income Tax for Medical Research and Development Institutions, etc. Located in High-Tech Medical Complexes)
(1) "Business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 159 (1) of the Act means a business related to health and medical technology under Article 2 (1) 1 of the Health and Medical Technology Promotion Act.

(2) "Cumulative investment amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 159 (3) 1 of the Act means the total investment amount under Article 116-27 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The amount of individual local income tax payable pursuant to Article 159 (5) of the Act shall be the amount calculated using the following formula (if the result is negative, it shall be deemed zero; where the number of regular employees decreases in three consecutive taxable years after the end of the taxable year for which a reduction or exemption was received, the amount for the third taxable year means the amount after subtracting the sum of the amounts paid in the first and second taxable years; where the number of regular employees decreases in two consecutive taxable years, the amount for the second taxable year means the amount after subtracting the amount paid in the first taxable year), and shall be paid as individual local income tax when filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased:

[Sum of tax amounts reduced or exempted under Article 159 (3) 2 of the Act for taxable years within the three years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the relevant enterprise's number of regular employees decreased] - [(Number of regular employees at the place of business eligible for a reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of regular employees decreased) × 1,000,000 won]

(4) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees under Article 159 (6) of the Act shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (12) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

(5) A person seeking a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax pursuant to Article 159 (7) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax reduction or exemption to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 116-27 (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 159 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 112 (Tax Credits for Increases in Gross Revenue, etc. of Copper Scrap, etc. Business Operators)
(1) Article 160 (1) 1 of the Act shall apply only to persons who have continuously conducted the relevant business for at least one year, counted backward from the last day of the taxable year immediately preceding the taxable year for which the tax credit is sought.

(2) Where the aggregate amount of gross income and deductible expenses subject to purchaser payment under Article 160 (1) of the Act changes, or the amount of the tax credit decreases as a result of a correction to the tax base and tax amount for the relevant taxable year, the amount shall be recalculated.

(3) A person seeking a tax credit under Article 160 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a tax credit for an increase in gross revenue, etc. and a statement of gross income and deductible expenses subject to purchaser payment prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return for individual local income tax on global income: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax credit to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 117-4 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a tax credit for individual local income tax under Article 160 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 113 (Tax Credits for Cash Receipt Merchants)
(1) "Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 161 (1) of the Act means two won.

(2) Matters necessary for the smooth operation of the cash receipt system, such as the methods of issuing cash receipts, the details to be entered therein, their forms, and the retention and submission of cash receipt payment records, shall be governed by Article 121-3 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) and (2), Article 121-3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of tax credits under Article 161 of the Act.

Article 114 (Tax Credits for Gold Bullion Traded on the Gold Spot Market)
(1) "Gold bullion prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part of Article 162 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means gold bullion under Article 121-7 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014>

(2) "Business operator prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part of Article 162 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means a business operator under Article 121-7 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Newly inserted on August 20, 2014>

(3) "Custodian prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part of Article 162 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means a custodian under Article 121-7 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Newly inserted on August 20, 2014>

(4) "Gold spot market prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part of Article 162 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means a market under Article 121-7 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Newly inserted on August 20, 2014>

(5) Where gold bullion under paragraph (1) is withdrawn from a custodian, the amount transacted on the gold spot market under the main clause of the part of Article 162 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs shall be the amount appraised under Article 121-7 (14) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014>

(6) "Special relationship prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of the part of Article 162 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means the relationship between related parties under Article 98 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act. <Amended on August 20, 2014>

(7) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (6), Article 121-7 of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the application of tax credits under Article 162 of the Act. <Newly inserted on August 20, 2014>

Article 115 (Tax Credits for Electronic Commerce in Petroleum Products)
(1) "Electronic settlement network prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 165 (1) of the Act means an electronic settlement network for petroleum products under Article 104-22 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) A person seeking an individual local income tax credit pursuant to Article 165 of the Act shall submit an application for a tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax credit to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment pursuant to Article 104-22 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a reduction of or exemption from individual local income tax under Article 165 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 116 (Tax Credits for Expenses for Verification of Faithful Reporting)
A person seeking application of Article 166 (1) of the Act shall, when submitting a certificate of verification of faithful reporting under Article 70-2 (1) of the Income Tax Act, submit an application for a tax credit for expenses for verification of faithful reporting prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment: Provided, That where the person applies for an income tax credit pursuant to Article 121-6 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the person shall be deemed also to have applied for a tax credit for individual local income tax under Article 166 of the Act. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 116-2 (Tax Credits for Electronic Filing of Individual Local Income Tax Returns)
(1) "Individual local income tax prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 167-3 (1) of the Act means individual local income tax on global income for which a final return of the tax base and tax amount is filed under Article 95 of the Local Tax Act, and individual local income tax on capital gains for which a preliminary return of the tax base and tax amount is filed under Article 103-5 of that Act.

(2) "Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 167-3 (1) of the Act means 2,000 won (where a person falling under an exception to the obligation to file a final tax base return under Article 73 of the Income Tax Act files a final tax base return, the smaller of the assessed tax amount additionally paid or refunded and 1,000 won).

Article 116-3 (Tax Credits for Employment of Residents of Areas Experiencing Population Decline)
(1) "Regular employees prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 167-5 (1) of the Act means workers who are domestic persons and have entered into employment contracts under the Labor Standards Act: Provided, That persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs shall be excluded:

1. Workers whose employment contract period is less than one year (excluding workers whose total employment contract period is at least one year due to successive renewals of the employment contract);

2. Part-time workers under Article 2 (1) 9 of the Labor Standards Act: Provided, That workers whose contractual working hours are at least 60 hours per month shall be deemed regular employees;

3. Executive officers falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 40 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act;

4. The largest shareholder or largest capital contributor of the relevant enterprise and the spouse of such person;

5. Lineal ascendants and descendants (including their spouses) of a person falling under subparagraph 4, and persons related by kinship under Article 1-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes;

6. Persons for whom withholding of wage and salary income tax is not verified by the wage and salary income withholding register under Article 196 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act (hereinafter in this Article referred to as the "wage and salary income withholding register") and for whom payment of any of the following amounts is also not verified:

(a) Employer contributions and employee contributions under Article 3 (1) 11 and 12 of the National Pension Act;

(b) Insurance premiums for workplace-based insured persons under Article 69 of the National Health Insurance Act.

(2) An enterprise seeking application of Article 167-5 (1) of the Act shall, in the taxable year in which the first anniversary of the employment date of a regular employee under that paragraph falls, submit an application for a tax credit and a statement of calculation of the tax credit prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by documents proving the grounds for receiving the tax credit, such as the employment contract and wage and salary income withholding register for each regular employee eligible for the tax credit, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, together with the tax base return.

SECTION 12 RESTRICTIONS ON SPECIAL LOCAL INCOME TAXATION, ETC. <Newly inserted on March 14, 2014>

Article 117 (Exclusion from Investment Tax Credits, etc.)
(1) "Amount equivalent to interest costs paid by the State, etc., calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 168 (1) 2 of the Act means the aggregate amount of interest costs under Article 123 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Amount equivalent to interest subsidies provided by the State, etc., calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 168 (1) 3 of the Act means the amount calculated under Article 123 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 118 (Scope of Underreported Income)
(1) "Underreported amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 169 (3) of the Act means the amount under Article 122 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Cases falling under circumstances prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 169 (4) 3 of the Act preceding its items means cases under Article 122 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 119 (Exclusion from Reductions or Exemptions for Investments in the Overconcentration Control Region of the Seoul Metropolitan Area, etc.)
(1) "Digital broadcasting equipment prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 171 (1) and in Article 171 (2) of the Act means broadcasting equipment under Article 124 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) "Information and communications equipment prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 171 (1) and in Article 171 (2) of the Act means switching equipment, transmission equipment, line equipment, and information processing equipment among the telecommunications equipment under Article 8 of the Regulations on the Accounting and Reporting of Telecommunications Business.

(3) "Investment in expansion prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 171 (1) of the Act means investment classified as specified in the subparagraphs of Article 124 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) "Industrial complex or industrial area prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 171 (1) of the Act means an industrial complex or industrial area under Article 124 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

Article 120 (Exclusion from Reductions or Exemptions, etc. for Tax Amounts Below the Minimum Tax Amount)
(1) "Tax amount additionally collected as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 172 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means an amount falling under either of the following subparagraphs:

1. An additional amount equivalent to interest where tax amounts reduced or exempted are additionally collected under the Act (including cases in which such amounts are added to individual local income tax and voluntarily paid or assessed and collected);

2. A tax amount added to individual local income tax and voluntarily paid or assessed and collected in the relevant business year where individual local income tax amounts reduced or exempted are additionally collected under the Act.

(2) "Tax credits, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the part of Article 172 (1) of the Act preceding its subparagraphs means tax credits, tax exemptions, and reductions or exemptions not listed in subparagraphs 1 and 2 of the same paragraph among reductions of or exemptions from individual local income tax.

(3) Where individual local income tax is corrected because the amount of individual local income tax reported by a taxpayer (including an amended return or a request for correction, etc. under the Framework Act on Local Taxes) falls below the tax amount calculated under Article 172 of the Act, the tax amount shall be calculated by disallowing the applicable reductions or exemptions in the following order (within the same subparagraph, in the order of the Articles listed in the subparagraphs of Article 172 (1) of the Act):

1. Tax credit amounts under Article 172 (1) 1 of the Act. In such cases, where the amounts reduced or exempted under the same Article include tax credits carried forward, the tax credits arising later shall be disallowed first;

2. Exemptions from and reductions of individual local income tax under Article 172 (1) 2 of the Act.

Article 121 (Carryforward of Tax Credits)
(1) The number of graduates of high schools tailored to industrial demand, etc. under Article 174 (3) 1 of the Act shall be the number of graduates under Article 136-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) The number of young workers under Article 174 (3) 2 of the Act shall be the number of young workers under Article 136-2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(3) The number of workers with disabilities under Article 174 (3) 2 of the Act shall be the number of workers with disabilities under Article 136-2 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(4) The number of workers aged 60 or older under Article 174 (3) 2 of the Act shall be the number of workers aged 60 or older under Article 136-2 (4) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(5) The scope of regular employees and the calculation of the number of regular employees specified in paragraphs (1) through (4) shall be governed by Article 23 (10) through (13) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act. <Amended on February 3, 2015>

Article 122 (Additional Collection of Tax Amounts Reduced or Exempted)
(1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 175 of the Act means cases falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 137 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act.

(2) The additional amount equivalent to interest under Article 175 of the Act shall be the amount calculated by multiplying the amount of the tax credit received by the period specified in subparagraph 1 and the rate specified in subparagraph 2:

1. The period from the day following the date of filing the tax base return for the taxable year for which the tax credit was received to the date of filing the tax base return for the taxable year in which a ground under Article 175 of the Act arose;

2. Three ten-thousandths per day.

CHAPTER IV SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 123 (Scope of Direct Use)
In applying provisions of the Act or other statutes or regulations on the reduction of or exemption from property tax on land, the scope of direct use shall include cases in which buildings or housing to be used for activities eligible for the relevant reduction or exemption are under construction. <Amended on December 31, 2020>

Article 123-2 (Calculation, etc. of Amounts Equivalent to Interest concerning Additional Collection of Acquisition Tax Reduced or Exempted)
(1) The amount equivalent to interest to be additionally paid under the main clause of Article 178 (2) of the Act shall be the amount calculated by multiplying the amount of tax reduced or exempted by the period specified in subparagraph 1 and the rate specified in subparagraph 2: <Amended on December 31, 2021; December 29, 2023>

1. The period from the day following the original payment deadline for acquisition tax on the real estate for which the reduction or exemption was received to the date on which a ground for additional collection arose: Provided, That where a ground for additional collection arises after a refund or appropriation under Article 60 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes, the period shall run from the applicable date specified in the subparagraphs of Article 43 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of that Act to the date on which the ground for additional collection arose;

2. The interest rate under Article 34 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on Local Taxes.

(2) "Unavoidable grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as bankruptcy" in the proviso to Article 178 (2) of the Act means any of the following grounds:

1. A declaration of bankruptcy;

2. Sale, donation, or use of the relevant real estate for another purpose due to a natural disaster or another comparable unavoidable ground.

Article 124 (Submission of Written Opinions on Local Tax Reductions or Exemptions)
(1) "Matters concerning special local taxation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 181 (3) of the Act means matters falling under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on December 30, 2010; January 1, 2013; March 23, 2013; March 14, 2014; November 19, 2014; December 31, 2015; July 26, 2017>

1. Matters concerning special local taxation whose period of application expires in the relevant taxable year;

2. Matters concerning special local taxation for which less than two years have elapsed since their entry into force;

3. Matters concerning special local taxation whose scope is proposed to be expanded;

4. Matters concerning special local taxation requiring reconsideration due to changes in project plans, etc. relating to local tax reductions or exemptions under Article 181 (2) of the Act;

5. Matters concerning special local taxation requiring reconsideration due to changes in corporations and organizations, etc. publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety in consultation with the heads of other central administrative agencies.

(2) "Special local taxation prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 181 (6) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Amended on December 31, 2018>

1. Where the annual average amount of local tax reductions or exemptions for the three years immediately preceding the year in which the period of application of the relevant special local taxation expires (or for the period since its establishment where less than three years have elapsed since the special local taxation was established) is at least 10 billion won;

2. Where it is necessary to evaluate two or more Articles providing for reductions or exemptions collectively by field;

3. Where local tax expenditure needs to be made more efficient through objective verification because the amount of local tax reductions or exemptions is expected to continue to increase;

4. Other cases in which the Minister of the Interior and Safety deems an evaluation of special local taxation necessary.

(3) "Cases in which special local taxation involving at least a certain amount prescribed by Presidential Decree is proposed to be newly introduced" in Article 181 (7) of the Act means cases in which the estimated amount of local tax reductions or exemptions expected to arise during the reduction or exemption period of the relevant proposed special taxation is at least 10 billion won (where the contents of existing special local taxation are changed, this means cases in which the expected additional reductions or exemptions during the reduction or exemption period of the relevant proposed special taxation, in addition to the amount of the existing special local taxation, are at least 10 billion won): Provided, That cases recognized by the Minister of the Interior and Safety as requiring introduction in response to economic or social circumstances shall be excluded. <Amended on December 30, 2016; July 26, 2017; December 29, 2017>

(4) Tax-related investigation and research institutions in the latter part of Article 181 (6) and in Article 181 (7) of the Act shall each be institutions falling under any of the following subparagraphs: <Newly inserted on December 31, 2015; December 30, 2016; July 26, 2017; December 29, 2017; December 31, 2018; January 15, 2020; December 31, 2020>

1. The local tax research institute under Article 151 of the Framework Act on Local Taxes;

2. Other institutions designated and publicly notified by the Minister of the Interior and Safety as having specialized personnel, investigation and research capabilities, etc. in relation to evaluations of the appropriateness of special local taxation, etc.;

2-2. Deleted. <December 31, 2020>

2-3. Deleted. <December 31, 2020>

3. Deleted. <December 31, 2020>

(5) Detailed criteria, procedures, and other matters necessary for evaluations of special local taxation under Article 181 (6) and (7) of the Act shall be prescribed by the Minister of the Interior and Safety. <Newly inserted on December 30, 2016; July 26, 2017; December 29, 2017>

Article 125 (Matters Excluded from Adjustment of Reduction or Exemption Rates by Local Governments)
"Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 182 (2) of the Act means matters prescribed in Articles 6, 17, and 29 of the Act. <Amended on March 14, 2014>

Article 126 (Applications for Reductions or Exemptions)
(1) A person intending to apply for a local tax reduction or exemption under the main clause of Article 183 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for a reduction or exemption prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, accompanied by documents proving the grounds for receiving the reduction or exemption, to the head of the local government having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment at the applicable time specified in the following subparagraphs: <Amended on December 31, 2020>

1. Local taxes for which a taxpayer files a return of the tax base and tax amount and pays the tax to the head of a local government: When filing the return of the tax base and tax amount for the relevant local tax: Provided, That where a determination or correction is requested under Article 50 (1) and (2) of the Framework Act on Local Taxes, the time shall be when that determination or correction is requested;

2. Local taxes other than those specified in subparagraph 1: The applicable time specified in the following items:

(a) The individual portion of resident tax, property tax (including amounts assessed under Article 112 of the Local Tax Act), and the fire-fighting portion of regional resource and facility tax: By the last day of the month in which the tax base date falls;

(b) Registration and license tax (limited to cases collected by ordinary collection under Article 35 (2) of the Local Tax Act), automobile tax under Article 125 (1) of that Act, and the specific resources portion of regional resource and facility tax (limited to cases collected by ordinary collection under the proviso to Article 147 (1) 1 of that Act): By the tenth day of the month in which payment is due.

(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), where acquisition tax and registration and license tax on a motor vehicle are to be reduced or exempted, the head of a Si/Gun/Gu who does not have jurisdiction over the principal place of use of the relevant motor vehicle may also handle the duties under paragraph (1). In such cases, those duties shall be deemed to have been handled by the head of the Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the principal place of use. <Amended on December 30, 2016; December 31, 2020>

(3) Where the head of a Si/Gun/Gu who does not have jurisdiction over the principal place of use of the relevant motor vehicle has handled the duties under paragraph (2), that head shall immediately forward all relevant documents to the head of the Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the principal place of use of the relevant motor vehicle. <Amended on December 30, 2016>

Article 127 (Submission of Data on Reductions or Exemptions)
A person required to submit data on local tax reductions or exemptions pursuant to Article 184 of the Act shall, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety, submit data that enables the verification of the objects eligible for reductions or exemptions, the amounts of tax reduced or exempted, etc. during the period from January 1 through December 31 of the relevant year to the head of the Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over the location of the taxable object by January 31 of the following year. <Amended on March 23, 2013; March 14, 2014; November 19, 2014; December 30, 2016; July 26, 2017>

Article 128 (Special Cases concerning Application of Reductions or Exemptions to Trust Property)
"Trust prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 185 of the Act means a trust under the Trust Act in which a trustee accepts and manages the settlor's real estate in trust to secure the performance of the settlor's obligations.

Article 129 (Special Cases concerning Application of Reductions or Exemptions in Areas Experiencing Population Decline)
"Regular employees prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 186 (3) 1 of the Act means regular employees under Article 116-3 (1).

